\qs*
\q1 \v 14 They return at evening;
\q2 they growl like a dog and go around the city.
\q1 \v 15 They, they wander around to eat.
\q2 If they are not full, then they lodge.
\q1 \v 16 But I, I will sing {about} your strength,
\q2 and I will sing aloud in the morning {about} your covenant faithfulness!
\q1 For you are a stronghold to me
\q2 and a refuge in the day of trouble to me.
\q1 \v 17 Let me make music to you, my strength,
\q2 for God {is} my stronghold, the God of my covenant faithfulness.
\c 60
\d For the chief musician; on “The Lily.” A testimony. A miktam of David, for teaching. When he fought with Aram Naharaim and with Aram Zobah, and Joab returned and struck Edom in the Valley of Salt, 12, 000.
\q1 \v 1 God, you have rejected us; you have broken through us.
\q2 You have become angry; restore us!
\q1 \v 2 You have made the earth tremble; you have broken it.
\q2 Heal its breaches, for it shakes.
\q1 \v 3 You have made your people see the difficult.
\q2 You have made us drink the wine of staggering.
\q1 \v 4 You have given a banner to the ones fearing you,
\q2 to be displayed from the face of the bow.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 5 So that your beloved may be delivered,
\q2 save {us} {with} your right hand and answer me.
\q1 \v 6 God has spoken in his holiness,
