\c 61
\d For the chief musician; on a stringed instrument. Of David.
\q1 \v 1 Hear my cry, God;
\q2 listen {to} my prayer.
\q1 \v 2 From the end of the earth I call to you when my heart is faint.
\q2 Lead me to the rock {that} is higher than me.
\q1 \v 3 For you are a refuge to me,
\q2 a strong tower from the face of the enemy.
\q1 \v 4 Let me sojourn in your tent forever!
\q2 I will take refuge in the shelter of your wings.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 5 For you, God, have listened to my vows.
\q2 You have given {me} the inheritance of the fearers of your name.
