\q1 \v 7 May he dwell forever to the face of God.
\q2 Appoint covenant faithfulness and truth; may they preserve him.
\q1 \v 8 Thus let me make music {to} your name forever,
\q2 that I may pay my vows day, day.
\c 62
\d For the chief musician; on Jeduthun. A psalm of David.
\q1 \v 1 Truly toward God my soul {is in} silence.
\q2 From him {is} my salvation.
\q1 \v 2 He alone {is} my rock and my salvation, my stronghold.
\q2 I will not be greatly shaken.
\q1 \v 3 Until when will you shout at a man?
\q2 You will be smashed, all of you,
\q2 like a leaning wall, an overthrown fence.
\q1 \v 4 They consult only to cast {him} down from his elevation.
\q2 They delight {in} a lie;
\q1 with his mouth, they bless,
\q2 but in their inside, they curse.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 5 Be silent, my soul, toward God alone,
\q2 for my hope is from him.
\q1 \v 6 He alone {is} my rock and my salvation, my stronghold.
\q2 I will not be shaken.
\q1 \v 7 In God {is} my salvation and my glory;
\q2 the rock of my strength, my refuge, {is} in God.
\q1 \v 8 Trust in him in every time, people.
\q2 Pour out your heart to his face.
\q2 God {is} a refuge for us.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 9 Surely sons of a human {are} vapor,
\q2 sons of a man {are} a lie.
\q1 To go up on the scales,
\q2 they together {would be lighter} than vapor.
\q1 \v 10 Do not trust in oppression,
\q2 and do not hope vainly in robbery.
\q2 Wealth, if it increases, do not set the heart.
\q1 \v 11 Once God has spoken, twice I have heard this,
\q2 that power {is} to God.
\q1 \v 12 Also to you, Lord, {is} covenant faithfulness,
\q2 for you, you repay to a man according to his doing.
\c 63
\d A psalm of David, when he was in the wilderness of Judah.
\q1 \v 1 God, you {are} my God. I seek you earnestly.
\q2 My soul thirsts for you, my flesh faints for you
\q2 in a land of dryness and weary, without water.
\q1 \v 2 Thus in the sanctuary I have gazed {at} you
\q2 to see your power and your glory.
\q1 \v 3 Because your covenant faithfulness {is} better than life,
\q2 my lips will praise you.
\q1 \v 4 Thus I will bless you in my life;
\q2 I will lift up my palms in your name.
\q1 \v 5 As {with} fat and fatness my soul will be full,
\q2 and {with} lips of joyful shouts my mouth will praise {you}.
\q1 \v 6 When I remember you on my bed,
\q2 I meditate on you in the night watches.
\q1 \v 7 For you have been a help to me,
\q2 and in the shadow of your wings I shout joyfully.
\q1 \v 8 My soul clings after you;
\q2 your right hand upholds me.
\q1 \v 9 But they, they seek my life for devastation;
\q2 they will come into the lowest parts of the earth.
\q1 \v 10 They will pour him into the hands of the sword;
\q2 they will be a portion of jackals.
\q1 \v 11 But the king will rejoice in God;
\q2 all of the swearers by him will exult,
\q2 for the mouth of speakers of falsehood will be shut.
\c 64
\d For the chief musician. A psalm of David.
\q1 \v 1 Hear my voice, God, in my complaint.
\q2 Preserve my life from fear of the enemy.
\q1 \v 2 Hide me from the council of evildoers,
\q2 from the throng of the workers of iniquity,
\q1 \v 3 who have sharpened their tongue like a sword.
\q2 They tread their arrow, a bitter word,
\q1 \v 4 to shoot the innocent from secret places;
\q2 suddenly they shoot, and they do not fear.
\q1 \v 5 They strengthen for themselves an evil matter;
\q2 they recount hiding snares.
\q2 They say, “Who will see them?”
\q1 \v 6 They devise iniquities.
\q2 “We have perfected a well-devised device!”
