\q1 \v 7 But God will shoot an arrow;
\q2 suddenly their wounds will happen.
\q1 \v 8 And they will make it stumble over them, their tongue.
\q2 Everyone seeing them will flee.
\q1 \v 9 And all of mankind will fear,
\q2 and they will declare the work of God,
\q2 for they will consider his deed.
\q1 \v 10 The righteous will rejoice in Yahweh and take refuge in him,
\q2 and all of the upright of heart will celebrate.
\c 65
\d For the chief musician. A psalm of David. A song.
\q1 \v 1 Praise {is in} silence toward you, God, in Zion,
\q2 and to you a vow will be paid.
\q1 \v 2 Hearer of prayer,
\q2 to you all flesh will come.
\q1 \v 3 Matters of iniquities prevail against me;
