\q1 \v 9 You visit the earth and saturate it;
\q2 you greatly enrich it.
\q2 The channel of God {is} full of water;
\q1 you prepare their grain,
\q2 for thus you prepare it.
\q1 \v 10 Watering its furrows,
\q2 settling its ridges,
\q1 you soften it with showers;
\q2 you bless its growth.
\q1 \v 11 You crown the year {with} your goodness,
\q2 and your tracks drip fatness.
\q1 \v 12 The pastures of the wilderness drip,
\q2 and the hills gird on rejoicing.
\q1 \v 13 The meadows put on a flock,
\q2 and the valleys cover {themselves} {with} grain.
\q1 They shout joyfully;
\q2 indeed, they sing.
\c 66
\p
\v 1 \d For the chief musician; a song; a psalm.
\q1 Shout to God, all of the earth!
\q1 \v 2 Make music {to} the glory of his name;
\q2 make his praise glorious.
\q1 \v 3 Say to God, “How fearsome {are} your deeds!
\q2 Because of the greatness of your power, your enemies cringe before you.
\q1 \v 4 All of the earth bows down to you
\q2 and makes music to you;
\q2 they make music {to} your name.”
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 5 Come and see the works of God,
\q2 fearsome in doing toward the sons of man.
\q1 \v 6 He turned the sea into dry land;
\q2 they passed through the river on foot.
\q2 There let us rejoice in him!
\q1 \v 7 He is ruling by his might forever;
\q2 his eyes watch over the nations.
\q2 Let the ones rebelling not exalt themselves.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 8 Bless our God, peoples,
\q2 and make the sound of his praise heard,
\q1 \v 9 the one putting our soul among the living,
\q2 and he does not allow our foot to slip.
\q1 \v 10 For you tested us, God;
\q2 you refined us like the refining of silver.
\q1 \v 11 You brought us into a net;
\q2 you put pressure on our loins.
\q1 \v 12 You made man ride over our head;
\q2 we went through fire and through waters,
\q2 but you brought us out to abundance.
\q1 \v 13 I will come {into} your house with burnt offerings;
\q2 I will pay my vows to you,
\q1 \v 14 {for} which my lips opened
\q2 and my mouth spoke when trouble {was} to me.
\q1 \v 15 I will offer up burnt offerings of fatlings to you
\q2 with the smoke of rams;
\q2 I will offer cattle with male goats.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 16 Come, listen, and let me recount,
\q2 all fearers of God,
\q2 what he has done for my soul.
\q1 \v 17 I called to him {with} my mouth,
\q2 and he was exalted from my tongue.
\q1 \v 18 If I had regarded iniquity in my heart,
\q2 the Lord would not have heard.
\q1 \v 19 Surely God has heard;
\q2 he has attended to the voice of my prayer.
\q1 \v 20 Blessed {be} God,
\q2 who has not turned away my prayer
\q2 or his covenant faithfulness from me.
\c 67
\d For the chief musician; on stringed instruments. A psalm. A song.
\q1 \v 1 May God be gracious to us and bless us;
\q2 may he make his face shine on us,
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 2 for the knowing of your way on the earth,
\q2 your salvation among all of the nations.
\q1 \v 3 May the peoples thank you, God;
\q2 may the peoples thank you, all of them.
\q1 \v 4 May the nations rejoice and shout joyfully,
\q2 for you judge the peoples {with} uprightness,
\q2 and the nations on the earth, you guide them.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 5 May the peoples thank you, God;
\q2 may the peoples thank you, all of them.
\q1 \v 6 The earth has given its produce;
\q2 may God, our God, bless us.
\q1 \v 7 May God bless us,
\q2 and may all of the ends of the earth fear him.
\c 68
\d For the chief musician. A psalm of David. A song.
\q1 \v 1 Let God arise, let his enemies scatter,
\q2 and let the ones hating him flee from his face.
\q1 \v 2 As smoke is driven away, drive {them} away;
\q2 as wax melts from the face of fire,
\q2 let the wicked perish from the face of God.
\q1 \v 3 But let the righteous rejoice, let them exult to the face of God,
\q2 and let them be glad with rejoicing.
\q1 \v 4 Sing to God, make music {to} his name,
\q2 lift up to the one riding over the plains.
\q2 In Yah {is} his name; yes, exult to his face.
\q1 \v 5 A father of orphans and a judge of widows
\q2 {is} God in the abode of his holiness.
\q1 \v 6 God is making the lonely dwell in a house;
\q2 he is bringing out prisoners into prosperity.
\q2 But the ones rebelling dwell in dryness.
\q1 \v 7 God, when you went out to the face of your people,
\q2 when you marched in the wilderness,
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 8 the earth quaked; indeed, the heavens dripped
\q2 from the face of God;
\q2 this Sinai, from the face of God, the God of Israel.
\q1 \v 9 A rain of generosities you shook out, God;
\q2 your inheritance, when it was wearied, you, you established it.
\q1 \v 10 Your flock dwelt in it;
\q2 in your goodness, you prepared for the poor, God.
\q1 \v 11 The Lord utters the word;
\q2 the {women} proclaiming good news {are} a great army.
\q1 \v 12 Kings of armies flee, they flee,
\q2 and the habitation of the house, she divides the spoil.
\q1 \v 13 Though you lie down between the sheepfolds,
\q2 the wings of a dove covered with silver
\q2 and its feathers, with greenness of gold.
\q1 \v 14 When Shaddai scattered kings in it,
\q2 it snowed on Zalmon.
\q1 \v 15 Mount Bashan {is} a mountain of God;
\q2 Mount Bashan {is} a mountain of peaks.
\q1 \v 16 Why do you look enviously, mountains, peaks,
\q2 {at} the mountain God desired for his dwelling?
\q2 Indeed, Yahweh will inhabit {it} forever.
\q1 \v 17 The chariotry of God {is} two myriads, thousands of repetition.
\q2 The Lord {is} among them; Sinai {is} in the holy {place}.
\q1 \v 18 You have ascended to the height,
\q2 you have taken captivity captive,
\q1 you have received gifts among men
\q2 and even {among} the ones rebelling,
\q2 that Yah God might dwell {there}.
\q1 \v 19 Blessed {be} the Lord! Day, day he bears for us,
\q2 the God of our salvation.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 20 God {is} to us a God of salvations,
\q2 and to Yahweh the Lord {are} exits from death.
\q1 \v 21 Surely God will crush the head of his enemies,
\q2 the pate of hair of the one walking ahead in his trespasses.
\q1 \v 22 The Lord said, “I will bring back from Bashan,
\q2 I will bring back from the depths of the sea,
\q1 \v 23 so that your foot may smash in blood,
\q2 the tongue of your dogs, its portion from the enemies.”
\q1 \v 24 They see your processions, God,
\q2 the processions of my God, my king, into the holy {place}.
\q1 \v 25 The singers go ahead; the ones playing stringed instruments, behind,
\q2 maidens playing timbrels, in the midst.
\q1 \v 26 Bless God in the assemblies,
\q2 Yahweh, from the fountain of Israel.
\q1 \v 27 There {is} Benjamin, the littlest,
\q2 ruling them; the princes of Judah, their throngs;
\q2 the princes of Zebulun, the princes of Naphtali.
\q1 \v 28 Your God has commanded your strength.
\q2 Be strong, God! You have done this for us.
\q1 \v 29 Because of your temple over Jerusalem,
\q2 kings will bring a gift to you.
\q1 \v 30 Rebuke the beast of the reed,
\q2 the assembly of the mighty with the calves of the peoples,
