\q1 \v 31 Nobles will come from Egypt;
\q2 Cush will make its hands run to God.
\q1 \v 32 Kingdoms of the earth, sing to God!
\q2 Make music {to} the Lord,
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 33 to the rider on the heavens, of the heavens of antiquity.
\q2 Behold, he utters with his voice, a voice of power.
\q1 \v 34 Ascribe strength to God;
\q2 his majesty {is} over Israel,
\q2 and his strength {is} in the clouds.
\q1 \v 35 God, {you are} fearsome from your sanctuary!
\q2 The God of Israel, he is giving strength and forces to the people.
\q2 Blessed {be} God!
\c 69
\d For the chief musician; on “Lilies”; of David
\q1 \v 1 Save me, God,
\q2 for waters have come up to {my} life.
\q1 \v 2 I have sunk in mire of depth,
\q2 and there is no standing.
\q1 I have come into depths of waters,
\q2 and a flood overflows me.
\q1 \v 3 I am weary in my calling out;
\q2 my throat is parched.
\q1 My eyes fail
\q2 {as} I am waiting for my God.
\q1 \v 4 The ones hating me gratuitously
\q2 are more than the hairs of my head.
\q1 The ones destroying me are mighty,
\q2 my enemies of falsehood.
\q1 What I did not steal,
\q2 yet I must restore.
\q1 \v 5 God, you, you know my foolishness,
\q2 and my sins are not hidden from you.
\q1 \v 6 May the ones waiting for you not have shame because of me,
\q2 Lord Yahweh of Armies.
\q1 May the ones seeking you not be humiliated because of me,
\q2 God of Israel.
\q1 \v 7 For because of you I have borne reproach;
\q2 humiliation has covered my face.
\q1 \v 8 I have become a stranger to my brothers
\q2 and a foreigner to the sons of my mother.
\q1 \v 9 For zeal for your house has consumed me,
\q2 and the reproaches of the ones reproaching you have fallen on me.
\q1 \v 10 Though I wept {in} my soul with fasting,
\q2 yet it became reproaches to me;
\q1 \v 11 though I made my clothing sackcloth,
\q2 yet I became a proverb to them.
\q1 \v 12 The sitters at the gate speak about me,
\q2 and the songs of the drinkers of beer.
\q1 \v 13 But I, my prayer {is} to you, Yahweh.
\q2 {At} a time of favor, God,
\q1 in the greatness of your covenant faithfulness,
\q2 answer me in the truth of your salvation.
\q1 \v 14 Deliver me from the mire, and let me not sink.
\q2 Let me be delivered from the ones hating me
\q2 and from the depths of the waters.
\q1 \v 15 Let the flood of waters not overflow me,
\q2 and let the deep not swallow me,
\q2 and let the pit not close its mouth over me.
\q1 \v 16 Answer me, Yahweh, for your covenant faithfulness {is} good;
\q2 according to the greatness of your compassion, turn to me.
\q1 \v 17 And may you not hide your face from your servant,
\q2 for trouble {is} to me; hurry, answer me.
\q1 \v 18 Draw near to my soul, redeem it;
\q2 because of my enemies, ransom me.
\q1 \v 19 You, you know my reproach
\q2 and my shame and my humiliation.
\q1 All of my adversaries {are} before you.
\q1 \v 20 Reproach has broken my heart,
\q2 and I am sick.
\q1 Though I waited for sympathy, yet there was none,
\q2 and for comforters, yet I did not find.
\q1 \v 21 But they put gall in my food,
\q2 and they made me drink vinegar for my thirst.
\q1 \v 22 Let their table become a snare to their faces
\q2 and a trap for their welfare.
\q1 \v 23 Let their eyes darken from seeing,
\q2 and make their loins tremble continually.
\q1 \v 24 Pour your indignation on them,
\q2 and let the burning of your nose overtake them.
\q1 \v 25 Let their encampment be deserted;
\q2 let there not be a dweller in their tents.
\q1 \v 26 For you, whom you have struck, they have persecuted,
\q2 and they talk about the pain of your wounded.
\q1 \v 27 Add iniquity to their iniquity,
\q2 and let them not come into your righteousness.
\q1 \v 28 Let them be wiped from the book of the living,
\q2 and let them not be written with the righteous.
\q1 \v 29 But I {am} poor and feeling pain;
\q2 may your salvation, God, set me on high.
\q1 \v 30 I will praise the name of God with a song,
\q2 and I will magnify him with thanksgiving.
\q1 \v 31 And this will be better to Yahweh than an ox,
\q2 a bull having horns and having hooves.
\q1 \v 32 The poor will see, they will rejoice;
\q2 seekers of God, let your heart live.
\q1 \v 33 For Yahweh is hearing the needy,
\q2 and he does not despise his prisoners.
\q1 \v 34 Let the heavens and the earth praise him,
\q2 the seas and everything moving in them.
\q1 \v 35 For God will save Zion,
\q2 and he will build the cities of Judah,
\q1 that they may dwell there and possess it.
\q1 \v 36 And the seed of his servants will inherit it,
\q2 and the ones loving his name will dwell in it.
\c 70
\d For the chief musician. Of David. To cause to remember.
\q1 \v 1 Hurry, God, to deliver me,
\q2 Yahweh, to my help!
\q1 \v 2 Let the ones seeking my life have shame and have confusion;
\q2 let the ones delighting in my harm be turned back and disgraced.
\q1 \v 3 Let them turn back on account of their shame,
\q2 the ones saying, “Aha! Aha!”
\q1 \v 4 Let all of the seekers of you rejoice and be glad in you,
\q2 and let the lovers of your salvation say continually, “God is great!”
\q1 \v 5 But I {am} poor and needy;
\q2 God, hurry to me!
\q1 You {are} my help and my deliverer;
\q2 Yahweh, do not delay!
\c 71
\q1 \v 1 In you, Yahweh, I take refuge;
\q2 let me not ever have shame.
\q1 \v 2 In your righteousness, deliver me and rescue me;
\q2 incline your ear to me and save me.
\q1 \v 3 Be to me a rock of abode for coming continually;
\q2 you command to save me,
\q2 for you {are} my rock and my stronghold.
\q1 \v 4 My God, rescue me from the hand of the wicked,
\q2 from the palm of the one doing wrong and the one being cruel;
\q1 \v 5 for you {are} my hope, Lord Yahweh,
\q2 my confidence from my youth.
\q1 \v 6 I have supported myself on you from the womb;
\q2 you were taking me from the belly of my mother.
\q2 My praise {is} about you continually.
\q1 \v 7 I have become like a wonder to many,
\q2 but you {are} my refuge of strength.
\q1 \v 8 Let my mouth be filled {with} your praise,
\q2 all of the day {with} your splendor.
\q1 \v 9 May you not cast me away in the time of old age;
\q2 may you not forsake me when my strength fails.
\q1 \v 10 For my enemies have spoken against me,
\q2 and the ones watching my life have consulted together,
\q1 \v 11 saying, “God has forsaken him;
\q2 pursue and seize him,
\q2 for there is none delivering.”
\q1 \v 12 God, may you not be far from me;
\q2 my God, hasten to my help.
\q1 \v 13 Let them shame and finish, the adversaries of my life;
\q2 let them cover {with} reproach and disgrace, the ones seeking my harm.
\q1 \v 14 But I, I will hope continually,
\q2 and I will add to all of your praise.
\q1 \v 15 My mouth will recount your righteousness,
\q2 all of the day, your salvation,
\q2 for I do not know the numbers.
\q1 \v 16 I will come in the forces of Lord Yahweh;
\q2 I will remember your righteousness, yours alone.
\q1 \v 17 God, you have taught me from my youth,
\q2 and to this I declare your wonderful doings.
\q1 \v 18 And also until old age and gray hair,
\q2 God, do not forsake me,
\q2 until I declare your arm to a generation,
\q2 your might to everyone {who} will come.
\q1 \v 19 For your righteousness, God, {is} to height,
\q2 {you} who do great {things};
\q2 God, who {is} like you?
\q1 \v 20 {You} who have made me see many and evil troubles,
\q2 may you return, may you revive me,
\q2 and may you return, may you bring me up from the depths of the earth.
\q1 \v 21 May you increase my greatness,
\q2 and may you turn around, may you comfort me.
\q1 \v 22 Also I, I will praise you with the instrument of the lute
\q2 {for} your faithfulness, my God;
\q2 Let me make music to you with the harp, Holy {One} of Israel.
\q1 \v 23 My lips will shout joyfully when I make music to you,
\q2 and my soul, which you have redeemed.
\q1 \v 24 Also my tongue will meditate {on} your righteousness all of the day,
\q2 for they will shame, for they will confound the ones seeking my harm.
\c 72
\p
\v 1 \d Of Solomon.
\q1 God, give your judgments to the king
\q2 and your righteousness to the son of the king.
\q1 \v 2 May he judge your people with righteousness
\q2 and your poor with justice.
\q1 \v 3 May the mountains bring peace to the people,
\q2 and the hills, in righteousness.
\q1 \v 4 May he judge the poor of the people;
\q2 may he save the sons of the needy,
\q2 and may he crush the oppressor.
\q1 \v 5 May they fear you with the sun
\q2 and to the face of the moon, generation of generations.
\q1 \v 6 May he come down like rain on mown grass,
\q2 like showers, a drenching of the earth.
\q1 \v 7 May the righteous flourish in his days,
\q2 and abundance of peace until the moon {is} not.
\q1 \v 8 May he rule from sea to sea
\q2 and from the River to the ends of the earth.
\q1 \v 9 May desert-dwellers kneel to his face,
\q2 and may his enemies lick the dust.
\q1 \v 10 May the kings of Tarshish and the coastlands return tribute;
\q2 may the kings of Sheba and Seba bring near a gift.
\q1 \v 11 And may all kings bow down to him;
\q2 may all nations serve him.
\q1 \v 12 For may he deliver the needy crying out
\q2 and the poor when no helper {is} to him.
\q1 \v 13 May he have pity on the weak and the needy,
\q2 and may he save the lives of the needy.
\q1 \v 14 May he redeem their life from oppression and from violence,
\q2 and may their blood be precious in his eyes.
\q1 \v 15 May he live! And may one give to him from the gold of Sheba,
\q2 and may one pray for him continually;
\q2 may they bless him all of the day.
\q1 \v 16 May there be an abundance of grain in the land;
\q2 on the head of the mountains may its fruit sway like Lebanon,
\q2 and may they flourish from the city like the grass of the earth.
\q1 \v 17 May his name be forever;
\q2 may his name continue to the face of the sun.
\q1 And may they be blessed by him;
\q2 may all of the nations acclaim him.
\q1 \v 18 Blessed {be} Yahweh God, the God of Israel,
\q2 the one doing wonders, he alone.
\q1 \v 19 And blessed {be} the name of his glory forever,
\q2 and let all of the earth be filled {with} his glory.
\q2 Amen and amen.
\q1 \v 20 The prayers of David son of Jesse are finished.
\c 73
\ms1 Book Three
\q1 \v 1 \d A psalm of Asaph
\q1 Surely God is good to Israel,
\q2 to those with a pure heart.
\q1 \v 2 But as for me, my feet almost slipped;
\q1 my steps almost were caused to slide out {from under me}
\q1 \v 3 because I was envious of the arrogant
\q1 {when} I saw the prosperity of the wicked.
\q1 \v 4 For {they have} no ropes until their death,
\q1 and their belly is fat.
\q1 \v 5 They {are} free from the trouble of man,
\q1 and with {the rest of} man they are not afflicted.
\q1 \v 6 Therefore pride is a necklace for them;
\q1 a garment of violence covers them.
\q1 \v 7 Their eyes bulge out from fatness;
\q1 the imaginations of {their} heart overflow.
\q1 \v 8 They mock and speak with evil of oppression;
\q1 they speak from an elevated place.
\q1 \v 9 They set their mouth in the heavens,
\q1 and their tongue goes through the earth.
\q1 \v 10 Therefore his people turn here,
\q1 and waters of a full {cup} are drained by them.
\q1 \v 11 And they say, “How does God know?
\q1 And is there knowledge in the Most High?”
\q1 \v 12 Behold, these wicked;
\q1 they are always at ease, they increase in wealth.
\q1 \v 13 Surely in vain I have kept my heart clean
\q1 and washed my hands in innocence.
\q1 \v 14 For I have been stricken all of the day
\q1 and punished every morning.
\q1 \v 15 If I had said, “I will recount such things,”
\q1 behold, I would have betrayed the generation of your children.
\q1 \v 16 And {when} I thought {how} to understand this,
\q1 it {was} troublesome in my eyes
\q1 \v 17 until I went into the sanctuaries of God,
\q1 {then} I discerned their end.
\q1 \v 18 Surely you set them in slippery places;
\q1 you make them fall to destruction.
\q1 \v 19 How they are {brought} to desolation as in a moment!
\q1 They come to an end, they perish by terrors.
\q1 \v 20 Like a dream after {one} awakes,
\q1 Lord, when you rouse {yourself}, you will despise their image.
\q1 \v 21 When my heart was embittered,
\q1 and I was pierced in my kidneys,
\q1 \v 22 I {was} stupid and I was not knowing;
\q1 I was an animal with you.
\q1 \v 23 Yet I {am} continuously with you;
\q1 you hold {me} by my right hand.
\q1 \v 24 You guide me with your counsel,
\q1 and afterward you will take me {to} glory.
\q1 \v 25 Whom have I in heaven {but you}?
\q1 And besides you {there is} nothing on the earth I desire.
\q1 \v 26 My flesh and my heart fail,
\q1 {but} God {is} the rock of my heart and my portion forever.
\q1 \v 27 For behold, those who are far from you will perish;
\q1 you destroy every one being unfaithful to you.
\q1 \v 28 But {for} me, the closeness of God for me {is} good.
\q1 I have made the Lord, Yahweh, my refuge
\q1 in order to recount all your works.
\c 74
\p
\v 1 \d A maskil. Of Asaph.
\q1 Why, God, have you rejected {us} forever?
\q2 {Why} does your nose smoke against the flock of your pasture?
\q1 \v 2 Remember your congregation {that} you acquired {in} antiquity,
\q2 {which} you redeemed, the tribe of your inheritance,
\q2 this Mount Zion on which you have dwelt.
\q1 \v 3 Lift up your feet to the destructions of perpetuity,
\q2 {to} all the enemy has damaged in the holy place.
\q1 \v 4 Your adversaries roared in the midst of your meeting place;
\q2 they set up their signs {as} signs.
\q1 \v 5 It was known like one bringing upward
\q2 axes in a thicket of trees.
\q1 \v 6 And now with hatchet and hammers
\q2 they have broken down its carvings altogether.
\q1 \v 7 They sent your holy place into fire;
\q2 they profaned the dwelling of your name to the ground.
\q1 \v 8 They said in their heart, “Let us oppress them altogether.”
\q2 They burned all of the meeting places of God in the land.
\q1 \v 9 We do not see our signs;
\q2 there is no longer a prophet
\q2 and not one with us knowing until when.
\q1 \v 10 Until when, God, will the adversary reproach?
\q2 Will the enemy despise your name forever?
\q1 \v 11 Why do you hold back your hand, even your right hand?
\q2 From the midst of your bosom finish {them}!
\q1 \v 12 But God {is} my king from antiquity,
\q2 working salvations in the midst of the earth.
\q1 \v 13 You, you divided the sea by your strength;
\q2 you broke the heads of the sea monsters in the waters.
\q1 \v 14 You, you crushed the heads of Leviathan;
\q2 you gave him {as} food to a people, to the desert-dwellers.
\q1 \v 15 You, you split open spring and wadi;
\q2 you, you dry up perpetual rivers.
\q1 \v 16 The day {is} to you; the night {is} also to you.
\q2 You, you established the light and the sun.
\q1 \v 17 You, you set all of the boundaries of the earth;
\q2 summer and winter, you, you formed them.
\q1 \v 18 Remember this: the enemy has reproached Yahweh,
\q2 and a foolish people has despised your name.
\q1 \v 19 May you not give the life of your dove to a beast;
\q2 may you not forget the life of your poor forever.
\q1 \v 20 Regard the covenant,
\q2 for pastures of violence fill the dark places of the land.
\q1 \v 21 May the weak not return ashamed;
\q2 may the poor and the needy praise your name.
\q1 \v 22 Arise, God! Plead your case!
\q2 Remember your reproach from the fool all of the day.
\q1 \v 23 Do not forget the voice of your adversaries,
\q2 the uproar of the ones rising against you, going up continually.
\c 75
\d For the chief musician; “May You Not Destroy.” A psalm of Asaph; a song.
\q1 \v 1 We give thanks to you, God;
\q2 we give thanks, and your name is near;
\q2 they recount your wonders.
\b
\q1 \v 2 When I take the appointed time;
\q2 I, I will judge {with} equity.
\q1 \v 3 The earth and all its inhabitants are melting;
\q2 I, I established its pillars.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\b
\q1 \v 4 I said to the boasters, “Do not boast,”
\q2 and to the wicked, “Do not lift up a horn.
\q1 \v 5 Do not lift up your horn to the height,
\q2 or speak with an arrogant neck.”
\b
\q1 \v 6 For not from the east or from the west,
\q2 and not from the wilderness {comes} lifting up.
\q1 \v 7 For God {is} the judge;
\q2 this one he brings low, and this one he lifts up.
\q1 \v 8 For a cup {is} in the hand of Yahweh,
\q2 and the wine foams, a full mixture,
\q2 and he pours out from this;
\q2 surely its dregs they will drain;
\q2 all the wicked of the earth will drink.
\b
\q1 \v 9 But I, I will declare to eternity;
\q2 I will sing praise to the God of Jacob.
\b
\q1 \v 10 “And all the horns of the wicked I will cut off;
\q2 the horns of the righteous will be lifted up.”
\c 76
\d For the chief musician; on stringed instruments. A psalm of Asaph, a song.
\q1 \v 1 In Judah God is known;
\q2 in Israel his name is great.
\q1 \v 2 And his abode is in Salem,
\q2 and his dwelling place is in Zion.
\q1 \v 3 There he broke the flames of the bow,
\q2 the shield, and the sword, and the battle.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\b
\q1 \v 4 You are shining, majestic,
\q2 from the mountains of prey.
\q1 \v 5 The stout of heart were plundered;
\q2 they slept their sleep,
\q2 and all of the men of strength found not their hands.
\q1 \v 6 At your rebuke, O God of Jacob,
\q2 both rider and horse fell deeply asleep.
\b
\q1 \v 7 You, you are to be feared,
\q2 and who can stand before your face from the time of your nose?
\q1 \v 8 From heaven you caused judgment to be heard;
\q2 the earth feared and was quiet
\q1 \v 9 when God arose to judgment,
\q2 to save all the humble of the earth.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\b
\q1 \v 10 For the wrath of man will thank you;
\q2 the remainder of wrath you will gird on.
\q1 \v 11 Vow and pay to Yahweh your God;
\q2 let all who are around him bring a gift to the Fear.
\q1 \v 12 He cuts off the spirit of princes;
\q2 he is to be feared by the kings of the earth.
\c 77
\d For the chief musician; on Jeduthun; a psalm of Asaph.
\q1 \v 1 My voice {is} to God, and I cry out;
\q2 my voice {is} to God, and he listens to me.
\q1 \v 2 In the day of my trouble I sought the Lord;
\q2 my hand was stretched out at night, and it did not slacken.
\q1 My soul refused to be comforted.
\q1 \v 3 I remembered God and I groaned;
\q2 I meditated, and my spirit grew faint.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 4 You held the lids of my eyes;
\q2 I was troubled and I did not speak.
\q1 \v 5 I thought about days from antiquity,
\q2 years of long ago.
\q1 \v 6 I will remember my song in the night;
\q2 with my heart I will meditate,
\q2 and my spirit searches.
\q1 \v 7 Will the Lord reject {me} forever?
\q2 And will he not again add to show favor?
\q1 \v 8 Has his covenant faithfulness ceased forever?
\q2 Has a promise ended for generation and generation?
\q1 \v 9 Has God forgotten to be gracious?
\q2 Or has he shut up his compassions in {his} nose?
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 10 And I said, “This is my wounding:
\q2 the changing of the right hand of the Most High.”
\q1 \v 11 I will remember the deeds of Yah;
\q2 for I will remember your wonder from antiquity.
\q1 \v 12 And I will ponder on all your deeds,
\q2 and on your works I will meditate.
\q1 \v 13 Your way, God, is in holiness;
\q2 what god is great like God?
\q1 \v 14 You are the God who does wonders;
\q2 you have revealed your strength among the peoples.
\q1 \v 15 You have redeemed your people with {your} arm,
\q2 the sons of Jacob and Joseph.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 16 The waters saw you, God;
\q2 the waters saw you, and they trembled;
\q2 indeed the depths shook.
\q1 \v 17 The clouds poured down water;
\q2 the skies gave a sound;
\q2 your arrows also flew about.
\q1 \v 18 The sound of your thunder {was} in the whirlwind;
\q2 the lightning lit up the world;
\q2 the earth trembled and shook.
\q1 \v 19 Your way went through the sea
\q2 and your path through many waters,
\q2 but your footprints were not discerned.
\q1 \v 20 You led your people like a flock
\q2 by the hand of Moses and Aaron.
\c 78
\p
\v 1 \d A maskil of Asaph.
\q1 Hear my teaching, my people;
\q2 incline your ears to the words of my mouth.
\q1 \v 2 I will open my mouth in a parable;
\q2 I will pour out riddles from antiquity.
\q1 \v 3 These are things that we have heard and learned,
\q2 things that our fathers have told us.
\q1 \v 4 We will not keep them from their descendants.
\q1 We will tell the next generation about the praises of Yahweh,
\q1 his strength, and his wonders that he has done.
\q1 \v 5 And he established a testimony in Jacob
\q2 and appointed a law in Israel,
\q1 which he commanded our fathers
\q1 to teach them to their children,
\q1 \v 6 So that the later generation might know, the children yet to be born,
\q1 and they will rise up and tell to their children.
\q1 \v 7 And they would place their confidence in God
\q2 and not forget the deeds of God
\q2 but keep his commandments.
\q1 \v 8 And they would not be like their fathers,
\q2 a stubborn generation and a rebellious generation,
\q2 {which} did not cause its heart to be steadfast,
\q2 and its spirit was not faithful with God.
\b
\q1 \v 9 The sons of Ephraim being armed {with} shooters of bows,
\q1 they turned back on the day of battle.
\q1 \v 10 They did not keep the covenant of God,
\q2 and they refused to walk in his law.
\q1 \v 11 And they forgot his deeds,
\q2 and his wonders that he had shown them.
\q1 \v 12 He did wonders before their fathers
\q1 in the land of Egypt, in the territory of Zoan.
\q1 \v 13 He divided the sea and led them across it,
\q2 and he made the waters to stand like a heap.
\q1 \v 14 And by day he led them with the cloud
\q2 and all the night with the light of fire.
\q1 \v 15 He split open the rocks in the wilderness,
\q2 and he gave drink abundantly as the deep.
\q1 \v 16 He made streams flow out of the rock
\q1 and made the water flow like rivers.
\q1 \v 17 And they added still to sin against him,
\q2 to rebel against the Most High in the dry land.
\q1 \v 18 And they tested God in their hearts
\q1 by asking {for} food for their appetite.
\q1 \v 19 And they spoke against God.
\q2 They said, “Can God arrange a table in the wilderness?
\q1 \v 20 Behold, he struck the rock
\q2 and waters gushed out
\q2 and streams overflowed.
\q1 Is he able to give bread also?
\q2 Or can he provide meat for his people?”
\q1 \v 21 Therefore, Yahweh heard and was furious,
\q2 and a fire was kindled against Jacob,
\q2 and also {his} nose went up against Israel,
\q1 \v 22 because they did not believe in God
\q2 and did not trust in his salvation.
\q1 \v 23 Yet he commanded the clouds from above
\q2 and opened the doors of the sky.
\q1 \v 24 And he rained down manna to eat on them,
\q2 and gave to them the grain of heaven.
\q1 \v 25 Man ate the bread of the mighty.
\q1 He sent to them provision to {their} satisfaction.
\q1 \v 26 He caused the east wind to blow in the sky,
\q1 and by his power he guided the south wind.
\q1 \v 27 And he rained down meat on them like dust,
\q2 and birds of wing as the sands of the sea.
\q1 \v 28 And he caused them to fall in the middle of his camp,
\q2 around his dwellings.
\q1 \v 29 And they ate and were very satisfied.
\q1 And he brought their craving to them.
\q1 \v 30 They were not separated from their craving,
\q2 their food was still in their mouth,
\q1 \v 31 and the nose of God went up in them
\q2 and he killed some of their stoutest people,
\q2 and he caused the young men of Israel to bow down.
\q1 \v 32 In all this they sinned again,
\q2 and did not believe in his wonders.
\b
\q1 \v 33 So he consumed their days in a vapor,
\q2 and their years in terror.
\q1 \v 34 When he killed them, then they would seek him,
\q2 and they would return and look earnestly for God.
\q1 \v 35 And they would remember that God was their rock
\q2 and {that} God Most High was their redeemer.
\q1 \v 36 And they would deceive him with their mouth
\q2 and lie to him with their tongues.
\q1 \v 37 And their hearts were not steadfast with him,
\q2 and they were not faithful in his covenant.
\q1 \v 38 Yet he, {being} merciful, atoned for their iniquity and did not destroy them.
\q2 And many times he held back his nose
\q2 and did not stir up all his wrath.
\q1 \v 39 And he remembered that they were flesh,
\q2 a wind going and it does not return.
\b
\q1 \v 40 How often they rebelled against him in the wilderness!
\q2 They grieved him in the desert!
\q1 \v 41 And they returned and they tested God
\q2 and grieved the Holy {One} of Israel.
\q1 \v 42 They did not remember his hand,
\q2 the day when he redeemed them from the adversary,
\q1 \v 43 when he set his signs in Egypt
\q2 and his wonders in the field of Zoan.
\q1 \v 44 And he turned their rivers to blood
\q2 and their streams they could not drink.
\q1 \v 45 He sent a swarm among them, and it devoured them,
\q2 and the frog and it destroyed them.
\q1 \v 46 And he gave their produce to the locust
\q2 and their labor to the swarming locust.
\q1 \v 47 He slew their vines with hail
\q2 and their sycamore trees with frost.
\q1 \v 48 And he gave over their cattle to the hail
\q2 and their livestock to the bolts of lightning.
\q1 \v 49 He sent among them the burning of his nose,
\q2 fury and indignation and distress,
\q2 a group of messengers of calamity.
\q1 \v 50 He made level a path for his anger;
\q2 he did not spare their soul from death,
\q2 and their life he gave over to the plague.
\q1 \v 51 And he struck every firstborn in Egypt,
\q2 the beginning of strength in the tents of Ham.
\q1 \v 52 And he made his people journey like sheep,
\q2 and he led them like a flock in the wilderness.
\q1 \v 53 And he guided them in security, and they did not fear,
\q2 and the sea covered their enemies.
\q1 \v 54 And he brought them to the border of his holiness,
\q2 this mountain that his right hand acquired.
\q1 \v 55 And he drove out nations from before them
\q2 and caused them to fall in a portion of inheritance,
\q2 and he caused the tribes of Israel to dwell in their tents.
\q1 \v 56 But they tested and rebelled against God Most High,
\q2 and they did not keep his testimonies.
\q1 \v 57 And they turned back and acted treacherously like their fathers;
\q2 they turned themselves like a bow of deceit.
\q1 \v 58 And they provoked him to anger with their high places,
\q2 and with their carved images they moved him to jealousy.
\q1 \v 59 God heard and was furious,
\q2 and he rejected Israel greatly.
\q1 \v 60 And he abandoned the dwelling of Shiloh,
\q2 the tent {in which} he had dwelt among mankind.
\q1 \v 61 And he gave his strength to captivity
\q2 and his splendor into the hand of the enemy.
\q1 \v 62 And he delivered his people over to the sword,
\q2 and he was furious with his inheritance.
\q1 \v 63 Fire consumed his young men,
\q2 and his virgins were not praised {in} wedding songs.
\q1 \v 64 His priests fell by the sword,
\q2 and his widows did not weep.
\q1 \v 65 Then the Lord awoke as one sleeping,
\q2 as a mighty man shouting from wine.
\q1 \v 66 And he struck his adversaries backward;
\q2 he gave to them a reproach of perpetuity.
\q1 \v 67 And he rejected the tent of Joseph,
\q2 and he did not choose the tribe of Ephraim.
\q1 \v 68 But he chose the tribe of Judah,
\q2 Mount Zion, which he loved.
\q1 \v 69 And he built his sanctuary like the heights,
\q2 like the earth he founded it forever.
\q1 \v 70 And he chose David his servant
\q2 and took him from the folds of the flock.
\q1 \v 71 From behind the nursing ewes he brought him,
\q2 to shepherd Jacob his people
\q2 and Israel his inheritance.
\q1 \v 72 And he shepherded them according to the integrity of his heart,
\q2 and with the skillfulness of his hands he guided them.
\c 79
\p
\v 1 \d A psalm. Of Asaph.
\q1 God, nations have come into your inheritance;
\q2 they have defiled the temple of your holiness;
\q2 they have made Jerusalem into heaps.
\q1 \v 2 They have given the corpse of your servants {as} food to the bird of the heavens,
\q2 the flesh of your faithful to the beast of the earth.
\q1 \v 3 They have poured out their blood like water around Jerusalem,
\q2 and there is no burying.
\q1 \v 4 We have become a reproach to our neighbors,
\q2 scorn and derision to the ones around us.
\q1 \v 5 Until when, Yahweh? Will you be angry forever?
\q2 Will your jealousy burn like fire?
\q1 \v 6 Pour out your wrath on the nations that have not known you
\q2 and on the kingdoms that have not called on your name.
\q1 \v 7 For one has devoured Jacob,
\q2 and they have desolated his habitation.
\q1 \v 8 Do not remember former iniquities against us;
\q2 hasten, let your compassions meet us,
\q2 for we have become very weak.
\q1 \v 9 Help us, God of our salvation, on account of the glory of your name, and deliver us
\q2 and cover over our sins for the sake of your name.
\q1 \v 10 Why should the nations say, “Where {is} their God?”
\q2 Let the vengeance of the poured-out blood of your servants
\q2 be known among the nations to our eyes.
\q1 \v 11 Let the groaning of the prisoner come to your face;
\q2 according to the greatness of your arm, preserve the sons of death.
\q1 \v 12 And return to our neighbors sevenfold, into their bosom,
\q2 their reproach {with} which they have reproached you, Lord.
\q1 \v 13 And we, your people and the flock of your pasture,
\q2 will give thanks to you forever;
\q2 to generation and generation we will recount your praise.
\c 80
\d For the chief musician; on “Lilies.” A testimony. Of Asaph; a psalm.
\q1 \v 1 Shepherd of Israel, give ear,
\q2 the one leading Joseph like a flock.
\q2 Sitter {on} the cherubim, shine forth.
\q1 \v 2 To the face of Ephraim and Benjamin and Manasseh,
\q2 awaken your might and come to us for salvation.
\q1 \v 3 God, restore us,
\q2 and make your face shine and let us be saved.
\q1 \v 4 Yahweh, God of armies,
\q2 until when will you smolder against the prayer of your people?
\q1 \v 5 You have made them eat bread of tears,
\q2 and you have made them drink tears {in} triple measure.
\q1 \v 6 You have made us strife to our neighbors,
\q2 and our enemies mock among themselves.
\q1 \v 7 God of armies, restore us,
\q2 and make your face shine and let us be saved.
\q1 \v 8 You pulled up a vine from Egypt;
\q2 you drove out nations and planted it.
\q1 \v 9 You cleared to the face of it,
\q2 and it rooted its roots and filled the land.
\q1 \v 10 The mountains were covered {with} its shadow,
\q2 and its branches {were} cedars of God.
\q1 \v 11 It sent out its branches to the sea,
\q2 and its shoots to the River.
\q1 \v 12 Why have you broken down its walls,
\q2 so that all the ones passing {on} the way pluck it?
\q1 \v 13 The boar from the forest ravages it,
\q2 and the creature of the field grazes on it.
\q1 \v 14 God of armies, return, please.
\q2 Look down from heaven and see,
\q2 and visit this vine,
\q1 \v 15 even the stock that your right hand planted,
\q2 and on the son you strengthened for yourself.
\q1 \v 16 It is burned with fire, it is cut down;
\q2 from the rebuke of your face they perish.
\q1 \v 17 Let your hand be on the man of your right hand,
\q2 on the son of man you strengthened for yourself.
\q1 \v 18 And we will not turn back from you;
\q2 revive us, and we will call on your name.
\q1 \v 19 Yahweh, God of armies, restore us.
\q2 Make your face shine, and let us be saved.
\c 81
\d For the chief musician; on Gittith; of Asaph.
\q1 \v 1 Shout joyfully to God, our strength;
\q2 shout out to the God of Jacob.
\q1 \v 2 Raise a song and put forth the tambourine,
\q2 the pleasant harp with the lyre.
\q1 \v 3 Blow a shofar at the new moon,
\q2 at the full moon for the day of our festival.
\q1 \v 4 For {it is} a statute for Israel,
\q2 a judgment of the God of Jacob.
\q1 \v 5 He set it as a testimony in Joseph
\q2 when he went out over the land of Egypt,
\q2 {where} I heard a lip I did not know.
\q1 \v 6 “I removed his shoulder from the burden;
\q2 his palms passed from the basket.
\q1 \v 7 In distress you called, and I delivered you;
\q2 I answered you from the secret place of thunder.
\q2 I tested you at the waters of Meribah.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 8 Hear, my people, and let me testify against you.
\q2 Israel, if you would listen to me!
\q1 \v 9 There shall not be a strange god among you,
\q2 and you shall not bow down to a god of foreignness.
\q1 \v 10 I {am} Yahweh your God,
\q2 the one having brought you up from the land of Egypt.
\q2 Open wide your mouth, and I will fill it.
\q1 \v 11 But my people did not listen to my voice,
\q2 and Israel did not submit to me.
\q1 \v 12 So I sent them away in the stubbornness of their heart;
\q2 they walked in their counsels.
\q1 \v 13 If only my people were listening to me,
\q2 {if} Israel would walk in my ways!
\q1 \v 14 As a little {thing} I would subdue their enemies,
\q2 and I would turn my hand against their adversaries.
\q1 \v 15 The haters of Yahweh would cringe before him,
\q2 and their time would be forever.
\q1 \v 16 And he would feed him with the fat of the wheat,
\q2 and I would satisfy you with honey from the rock.”
\c 82
\p
\v 1 \d A psalm. Of Asaph.
\q1 God is standing in the congregation of God;
\q2 in the midst of gods he judges:
\q1 \v 2 “Until when will you judge {with} injustice
\q2 and lift up the faces of the wicked?
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 3 Judge the poor and the orphan;
\q2 vindicate the poor and the destitute.
\q1 \v 4 Rescue the poor and the needy;
\q2 deliver {them} from the hand of the wicked.
\q1 \v 5 They do not know and they do not understand;
\q2 they walk about in darkness.
\q2 All of the foundations of the earth are shaken.
\q1 \v 6 I, I said, ‘You {are} gods
\q2 and sons of the Most High, all of you.
\q1 \v 7 But you will die like man,
\q2 and like one of the princes, you will fall.’”
\q1 \v 8 Arise, God, judge the earth,
\q2 for you, you will inherit among all of the nations.
\c 83
\d A song. A psalm. Of Asaph.
\q1 \v 1 God, {may} silence not {be} to you;
\q2 do not be still, and do not be quiet, God!
\q1 \v 2 For behold, your enemies roar,
\q2 and the ones hating you lift up {the} head.
\q1 \v 3 They are cunning {with} counsel against your people,
\q2 and they conspire against your treasured ones.
\q1 \v 4 They have said, “Come, and let us destroy them from {being} a nation,
\q2 that the name of Israel may not be remembered anymore.”
\q1 \v 5 For they have conspired against you, heart together;
\q2 they have cut a covenant:
\q1 \v 6 the tents of Edom and the Ishmaelites,
\q2 Moab and the Hagrites,
\q1 \v 7 Gebal and Ammon and Amalek,
\q2 Philistia with the dwellers of Tyre.
\q1 \v 8 Also Assyria has joined with them;
\q2 they {are} an arm to the sons of Lot.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 9 Do to them as {to} Midian,
\q2 as {to} Sisera, as {to} Jabin at the river of Kishon.
\q1 \v 10 They were destroyed at En Dor;
\q2 they became dung for the ground.
\q1 \v 11 Make them, their nobles, like Oreb and like Zeeb
\q2 and like Zebah and like Zalmunna, all of their princes,
\q1 \v 12 who said, “Let us possess for ourselves
\q2 the pastures of God.”
\q1 \v 13 My God, make them like tumbleweed,
\q2 like chaff to the face of the wind.
\q1 \v 14 As fire burns a forest,
\q2 and as flame kindles mountains,
\q1 \v 15 thus pursue them with your tempest,
\q2 and terrify them with your whirlwind.
\q1 \v 16 Fill their faces {with} shame,
\q2 that they may seek your name, Yahweh.
\q1 \v 17 May they have shame and be terrified, eternities of eternity,
\q2 and may they have disgrace and may they perish.
\q1 \v 18 And may they know that you, your name {is} Yahweh,
\q2 you alone {are} the Most High over all of the earth.
\c 84
\d For the chief musician; on Gittith. Of the sons of Korah. A psalm.
\q1 \v 1 How amiable {are} your dwellings,
\q2 Yahweh of Armies!
\q1 \v 2 My soul longs and even faints
\q2 for the courts of Yahweh;
\q1 my heart and my flesh cry out
\q2 to the living God.
\q1 \v 3 Even the sparrow has found a house,
\q2 and the swallow, a nest for herself,
\q2 where she may lay her young—
\q1 your altars, Yahweh of Armies,
\q2 my king and my God.
\q1 \v 4 The happinesses of the dwellers of your house!
\q2 They praise you continually.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 5 The happinesses of the man, strength to him {is} in you!
\q2 Highways {are} in their heart.
\q1 \v 6 Passing through in the Valley of Baca,
\q2 they make it a spring;
\q1 the early rain also covers {it} {with} blessings.
\q1 \v 7 They go from strength to strength;
\q2 {each} one appears before God in Zion.
\q1 \v 8 Yahweh, God of armies, hear my prayer;
\q2 listen, God of Jacob.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 9 See our shield, God,
\q2 and regard the face of your anointed.
\q1 \v 10 For a day in your courts {is} better than a thousand.
\q1 I choose to stand at the threshold in the house of my God
\q2 {rather} than dwell in the tents of wickedness.
\q1 \v 11 For Yahweh God {is} a sun and a shield;
\q2 Yahweh gives favor and glory.
\q1 He does not withhold good
\q2 from the ones walking in blamelessness.
\q1 \v 12 Yahweh of Armies,
\q2 the happinesses of the man trusting in you!
\c 85
\d For the chief musician. Of the sons of Korah. A psalm.
\q1 \v 1 You favored your land, Yahweh;
\q2 you restored the captivity of Jacob.
\q1 \v 2 You bore the iniquity of your people;
\q2 you covered all of their sin.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 3 You gathered up all of your wrath;
\q2 you turned back from the burning of your nose.
\q1 \v 4 Restore us, God of our salvation,
\q2 and break up your vexation with us.
\q1 \v 5 Will you be angry with us forever?
\q2 Will you prolong your nose to generation and generation?
\q1 \v 6 You, will you not return?
\q2 May you revive us, that your people may rejoice in you.
\q1 \v 7 Make us see your covenant faithfulness, Yahweh,
\q2 and give your salvation to us.
\q1 \v 8 Let me hear what God Yahweh will speak,
\q2 for he will speak peace to his people and to his faithful ones,
\q2 but let them not return to folly.
\q1 \v 9 Surely his salvation {is} near to his reverent {ones},
\q2 for glory to dwell in our land.
\q1 \v 10 Covenant faithfulness and truth will meet together;
\q2 righteousness and peace will kiss.
\q1 \v 11 Truth will sprout from the earth,
\q2 and righteousness will look down from the heavens.
\q1 \v 12 Also, Yahweh will give the good,
\q2 and our land will give its produce.
\q1 \v 13 Righteousness walks before him,
\q2 and it puts his steps in the way.
\c 86
\p
\v 1 \d A prayer. Of David.
\q1 Incline your ear, Yahweh;
\q2 answer me, for I {am} poor and needy.
\q1 \v 2 Guard my soul, for I {am} faithful.
\q1 You, my God, save your servant,
\q2 the one trusting in you.
\q1 \v 3 Favor me, Lord,
\q2 for to you I call all of the day.
\q1 \v 4 Gladden the soul of your servant,
\q2 for to you, Lord, I lift up my soul.
\q1 \v 5 For you, Lord, {are} good and forgiving
\q2 and plentiful of covenant faithfulness to all of the ones calling on you.
\q1 \v 6 Listen {to} my prayer, Yahweh,
\q2 and attend to the voice of my pleas.
\q1 \v 7 In the day of my trouble I call on you,
\q2 for you will answer me.
\q1 \v 8 There is none like you among the gods, Lord,
\q2 and there is nothing like your works.
\q1 \v 9 All of the nations that you have made
\q2 will come and bow down to your face, Lord,
\q2 and they will glorify your name.
\q1 \v 10 For you {are} great and are doing wonderful things;
\q2 you {are} God, you alone.
\q1 \v 11 Teach me your way, Yahweh.
\q2 that I may walk in your truth.
\q2 Unite my heart to fear your name.
\q1 \v 12 I will thank you, Lord my God, with all of my heart,
\q2 and I will glorify your name forever.
\q1 \v 13 For your covenant faithfulness {is} great toward me,
\q2 and you have delivered my soul from lowest Sheol.
\q1 \v 14 God, the arrogant arise against me,
\q2 and the congregation of the violent seek my life,
\q2 and they do not set you before them.
\q1 \v 15 But you, Lord, {are} a merciful and gracious God,
\q2 long of nostrils and plentiful of covenant faithfulness and truth.
\q1 \v 16 Turn to me and favor me;
\q2 give your strength to your servant,
\q2 and save the son of your female servant.
\q1 \v 17 Work for me a sign for good,
\q2 that the ones hating me may see and have shame,
\q2 for you, Yahweh, you help me and comfort me.
\c 87
\p
\v 1 \d Of the sons of Korah. A psalm. A song.
\q1 His foundation {is} on the mountains of holiness.
\q1 \v 2 Yahweh is loving the gates of Zion
\q2 more than all of the dwellings of Jacob.
\q1 \v 3 Glorious things are spoken of you,
\q2 city of God.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 4 I will mention Rahab and Babylon
\q2 to the ones knowing me;
\q1 behold, Philistia and Tyre
\q2 with Cush—
\q1 “This one was born there.”
\q1 \v 5 And of Zion it will be said,
\q2 “Man and man was born in her,
\q1 and he, he will establish her,
\q2 the Most High.”
\q1 \v 6 Yahweh will recount in the writing of the peoples,
\q2 “This {one} was born there.”
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 7 And the singers, like the pipers,
\q2 “All of my springs {are} in you.”
\c 88
\d A song. A psalm. Of the sons of Korah. For the chief musician. On “Weakness of Afflicting.” A maskil of Heman the Ezrahite.
\q1 \v 1 Yahweh, God of my salvation,
\q2 {by} day, in the night, I cry out before you.
\q1 \v 2 Let my prayer come to your face;
\q2 incline your ear to my cry.
\q1 \v 3 For my soul is full of troubles,
\q2 and my life has come near to Sheol.
\q1 \v 4 I am reckoned with the ones going down {into} the pit;
\q2 I have become like a man without strength,
\q1 \v 5 free among the ones having died,
\q2 like the slain lying in the grave,
\q2 whom you do not remember them anymore,
\q2 and they, they are cut off from your hand.
\q1 \v 6 You have set me in the pit of the depths,
\q2 in dark places, in deep places.
\q1 \v 7 Your wrath rests heavily on me,
\q2 and you overwhelm {me} {with} all of your waves.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 8 You have distanced my acquaintances from me;
\q2 you have made me abominations to them.
\q2 {I am} shut in, and I do not go out.
\q1 \v 9 My eye mourns from affliction.
\q2 I call out to you, Yahweh, in all of the day;
\q2 I spread out my palms to you.
\q1 \v 10 Will you do a wonder for the ones having died?
\q2 Or will the Raphaites arise? Will they thank you?
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 11 Will your covenant faithfulness be recounted in the grave,
\q2 your faithfulness in Abaddon?
\q1 \v 12 Will your wonder be known in the darkness,
\q2 or your righteousness, in the land of forgetfulness?
\q1 \v 13 But I, I cry out to you, Yahweh,
\q2 and in the morning my prayer precedes you.
\q1 \v 14 Why, Yahweh, do you reject my soul?
\q2 {Why} do you hide your face from me?
\q1 \v 15 I {have been} weak and expiring since youth;
\q2 I have borne your terrors; I must despair.
\q1 \v 16 Your indignations pass over me;
\q2 your terrors destroy me.
\q1 \v 17 They surround me like water all of the day;
\q2 they close in upon me together.
\q1 \v 18 You have distanced friend and acquaintance from me;
\q2 the ones known to me {are} darkness.
\c 89
\d A maskil. Of Ethan the Ezrahite.
\q1 \v 1 I will sing the covenant faithfulness of Yahweh forever;
\q2 to generation and generation I will make known your faithfulness with my mouth.
\q1 \v 2 For I said, “Covenant faithfulness will be built up forever;
\q2 the heavens, you establish your faithfulness in them.”
\q1 \v 3 “I have cut a covenant with my chosen;
\q2 I have sworn to David my servant:
\q1 \v 4 ‘Until forever I will establish your seed,
\q2 and I will build up your throne to generation and generation.’”
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 5 And the heavens praise your wonder, Yahweh;
\q2 your faithfulness also, in the assembly of the holy ones.
\q1 \v 6 For who in the sky arrays with Yahweh,
\q2 compares to Yahweh among the sons of God?
\q1 \v 7 God is greatly dreaded in the council of the holy ones
\q2 and feared above all of the ones around him.
\q1 \v 8 Yahweh, God of Armies,
\q2 who {is} like you, mighty Yah?
\q2 And your faithfulness {is} your surroundings.
\q1 \v 9 You are ruling over the surging of the sea;
\q2 when its waves rise, you, you still them.
\q1 \v 10 You, you shattered Rahab like a slain one;
\q2 with the arm of your strength you scattered your enemies.
\q1 \v 11 To you {are} the heavens, also to you, the earth;
\q2 the world and its fullness, you, you founded them.
\q1 \v 12 The north and the south, you, you created them;
\q2 Tabor and Hermon shout joyfully in your name.
\q1 \v 13 To you {is} an arm with might;
\q2 your hand is strong; your right hand is high.
\q1 \v 14 Righteousness and justice {are} the foundation of your throne;
\q2 covenant faithfulness and truth precede your face.
\q1 \v 15 The happinesses of the people knowing the joyful shout!
\q2 Yahweh, they walk in the light of your face.
\q1 \v 16 In your name they rejoice all of the day,
\q2 and in your righteousness they rise high;
\q1 \v 17 for you {are} the splendor of their strength,
\q2 and by your favor you raise up our horn.
\q1 \v 18 For our shield {is} to Yahweh,
\q2 and our king, to the Holy {One} of Israel.
\q1 \v 19 Then you spoke in a vision to your faithful ones and said,
\q2 “I have placed help on a warrior;
\q2 I have raised up a chosen one from the people.
\q1 \v 20 I have found David my servant;
\q2 I have anointed him with the oil of my holiness,
\q1 \v 21 with whom my hand will be established;
\q2 my arm will also strengthen him.
\q1 \v 22 The enemy will not exact from him,
\q2 and a son of wickedness will not oppress him.
\q1 \v 23 And I will crush his adversaries from his face,
\q2 and I will strike down the ones hating him.
\q1 \v 24 And my faithfulness and my covenant faithfulness {will be} with him,
\q2 and in my name his horn will be high.
\q1 \v 25 And I will set his hand on the sea
\q2 and his right hand on the rivers.
\q1 \v 26 He, he will call to me, ‘You {are} my Father,
\q2 my God and the rock of my salvation.’
\q1 \v 27 And I, I will make him the firstborn,
\q2 the highest of the kings of the earth.
\q1 \v 28 I will keep my covenant faithfulness for him forever,
\q2 and my covenant will be confirmed to him.
\q1 \v 29 And I will set up his seed forever
\q2 and his throne like the days of the heavens.
\q1 \v 30 If his sons forsake my law
\q2 and they do not walk in my judgments,
\q1 \v 31 if they profane my statutes
\q2 and they do not keep my commandments,
\q1 \v 32 then I will punish their transgression with a rod
\q2 and their iniquity with blows.
\q1 \v 33 But my covenant faithfulness I will not break off from him,
\q2 and I will not deal falsely in my faithfulness.
\q1 \v 34 I will not profane my covenant,
\q2 and I will not change the utterance of my lips
\q1 \v 35 Once I have sworn by my holiness,
\q2 ‘If I should lie to David!
\q1 \v 36 His seed will be forever,
\q2 and his throne, like the sun before me.
\q1 \v 37 It will be established forever like the moon,
\q2 yes, the attested witness in the sky.’”
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 38 But you, you have rejected and spurned;
\q2 you have passed yourself over from your anointed one.
\q1 \v 39 You have voided the covenant of your servant;
\q2 you have profaned his crown to the ground.
\q1 \v 40 You have broken down all of his walls;
\q2 you have made his fortifications a ruin.
\q1 \v 41 All of the passers of the way plunder him;
\q2 he has become a reproach to his neighbors.
\q1 \v 42 You have raised up the right hand of his adversaries;
\q2 you have made all of his enemies rejoice.
\q1 \v 43 You have also turned back the edge of his sword,
\q2 and you have not made him stand in battle.
\q1 \v 44 You have made his splendor cease,
\q2 and you have cast his throne to the ground.
\q1 \v 45 You have shortened the days of his youth;
\q2 you have covered him over with shame.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 46 Until when, Yahweh? Will you hide yourself forever?
\q2 Will your wrath burn like fire?
\q1 \v 47 Remember me, what life {is},
\q2 for what emptiness you created all of the sons of man.
\q1 \v 48 What man will live and not see death,
\q2 will deliver his soul from the hand of Sheol?
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 49 Where {are} your former covenant faithfulnesses, Lord,
\q2 {which} you swore to David in your faithfulness?
\q1 \v 50 Remember, Lord, the reproach of your servants;
\q2 my carrying in my bosom all of many peoples
\q1 \v 51 with which your enemies have taunted, Yahweh,
\q2 with which they have taunted the footsteps of your anointed.
\q1 \v 52 Blessed {be} Yahweh forever!
\q2 Amen and amen.
\c 90
\ms1 Book Four
\d A prayer of Moses, the man of God.
\q1 \v 1 Lord, you have been a habitation to us
\q1 in generation and generation.
\q1 \v 2 Before the mountains were born
\q1 or you brought forth the earth and the world,
\q1 even from forever to forever, you {are} God.
\q1 \v 3 You cause man to return to dust,
\q1 and you say, “Return, sons of man.”
\q1 \v 4 For a thousand years in your eyes
\q1 {are} like the day before when it has passed,
\q1 and a watch in the night.
\q1 \v 5 You flood them away—they are sleep;
\q1 in the morning, like grass, it passes along.
\q1 \v 6 In the morning it sprouts and passes along;
\q1 in the evening it withers and dries up.
\q1 \v 7 For by your nose, we perish,
\q1 and by your wrath we are terrified.
\q1 \v 8 You have set our iniquities before you,
\q1 our hidden {sin} in the light of your face.
\q1 \v 9 For all of our days turn in your wrath;
\q1 we end our years like a sigh.
\q1 \v 10 The days of our years, in them {are} 70 years,
\q1 or, if by strength, 80 years
\q1 but their expanse is trouble and sorrow,
\q1 for it passes quickly, and we fly away.
\q1 \v 11 Who knows the power of your nose,
\q1 or your wrath according to your fear?
\q1 \v 12 So teach {us} to number our days
\q1 that we might bring in a heart of wisdom.
\q1 \v 13 Return, Yahweh! Until when?
\q1 Have compassion on your servants.
\q1 \v 14 Satisfy us in the morning {with} your covenant faithfulness
\q1 and we will rejoice and be glad in all of our days.
\q1 \v 15 Make us glad according to the days you afflicted us
\q1 the years we have seen trouble.
\q1 \v 16 May your work be seen by your servants,
\q1 and your majesty by their sons.
\q1 \v 17 May the favor of the Lord our God be upon us.
\q1 And the work of our hands, establish for us;
\q1 indeed, the work of our hands, establish it.
\c 91
\q1 \v 1 The one dwelling in the shelter of the Most High
\q1 will remain in the shadow of Shaddai.
\q1 \v 2 I will say to Yahweh, “My refuge and my fortress,
\q1 my God, I trust in him.”
\q1 \v 3 For he will rescue you from the snare of the trapper,
\q1 from the plague of calamities.
\q1 \v 4 He will cover you with his feathers,
\q1 and under his wings you will shelter.
\q1 His faithfulness {is} a shield and rampart.
\q1 \v 5 You will not be afraid of the terror of the night,
\q1 of the arrow {that} flies by day,
\q1 \v 6 of the plague {that} walks in darkness,
\q1 of the destruction that wastes {at} midday.
\q1 \v 7 A thousand may fall at your side,
\q1 and a myriad at your right hand;
\q1 it will not approach toward you.
\q1 \v 8 You will only observe with your eyes
\q1 and see the recompense of the wicked.
\q1 \v 9 Because you have made Yahweh, my refuge,
\q1 the Most High, your dwelling,
\q1 \v 10 evil will not happen to you,
\q1 and a plague will not approach your tent.
\q1 \v 11 For he will command his angels concerning you,
\q1 to guard you in all of your ways.
\q1 \v 12 They will lift you up in their hands,
\q1 lest you hit your foot against a stone.
\q1 \v 13 You will tread on the lion and the adder;
\q1 you will trample the young lion and the serpent.
\q1 \v 14 “Because he clings to me, indeed I will deliver him.
\q1 I will protect him because he knows my name.
\q1 \v 15 He will call me and I will answer him.
\q1 I {will be} with him in trouble;
\q1 I will rescue him and I will honor him.
\q1 \v 16 I will satisfy him {with} length of days,
\q1 and I will show him my salvation.”
\c 92
\d A psalm, a song for the Sabbath day.
\q1 \v 1 It is good to give thanks to Yahweh
\q1 and to sing praises to your name, Most High,
\q1 \v 2 to proclaim your covenant faithfulness in the morning
\q1 and your truthfulness in the nights,
\q1 \v 3 with a ten {string}
\q1 and with a lyre;
\q1 with a melody on a harp.
\q1 \v 4 For you, Yahweh, have made me glad through your deeds.
\q1 I will sing for joy because of the deeds of your hands.
\q1 \v 5 How great are your deeds, Yahweh!
\q1 Your thoughts are very deep.
\q1 \v 6 A brutish person does not know,
\q1 nor does a stupid {one} understand this:
\q1 \v 7 When the wicked sprout like grass,
\q1 and all evildoers thrive,
\q1 they will be destroyed for eternity.
\q1 \v 8 But you, Yahweh, {are} exalted forever.
\q1 \v 9 For behold your enemies, Yahweh!
\q1 For behold your enemies—they will perish!
\q1 All those who do evil will be scattered.
\q1 \v 10 But you have lifted up my horn like a wild ox;
\q1 I am saturated with fresh oil.
\q1 \v 11 My eye has looked on my foes, those rising up against me;
\q1 those doing evil my ears have heard.
\q1 \v 12 The righteous {one} will flourish like the palm tree;
\q1 he will grow like a cedar in Lebanon.
\q1 \v 13 They are planted in the house of Yahweh;
\q1 they flourish in the courts of our God.
\q1 \v 14 They bear fruit even when they are old;
\q1 they are juicy and green,
\q1 \v 15 to proclaim that Yahweh is just,
\q1 my rock, and {there is} no unrighteousness in him.
\c 93
\q1 \v 1 Yahweh reigns; he wears majesty;
\q1 Yahweh wears, he girds himself with, strength.
\q1 Indeed, the world is firmly established; it cannot be moved.
\q1 \v 2 Your throne is established from before;
\q1 you are from everlasting.
\q1 \v 3 The seas rise, Yahweh;
\q1 the seas have lifted up their voice;
\q1 the seas lift up their pounding {waves}.
\q1 \v 4 More than the sounds of many waters,
\q1 than the mighty breakers of the sea,
\q1 Yahweh on high is mighty.
\q1 \v 5 Your decrees are very trustworthy;
\q1 holiness adorns your house,
\q1 Yahweh, for length of days.
\c 94
\q1 \v 1 God of vengeance,
\q1 Yahweh, God of vengeance,
\q1 shine forth!
\v 2 Rise up, judge of the earth,
\q1 return recompense upon the proud.
\q1 \v 3 Until when will the wicked, Yahweh,
\q1 until when will the wicked rejoice?
\q1 \v 4 They pour out, they speak, arrogance;
\q1 all doers of evil praise themselves.
\q1 \v 5 They crush your people, Yahweh;
\q1 they afflict your inheritance.
\q1 \v 6 They kill the widow and the sojourner,
\q1 and they murder the fatherless.
\q1 \v 7 They say, “Yah does not see,
\q1 the God of Jacob does not perceive.”
\q1 \v 8 Understand, stupid ones among the people!
\q1 O fools, when will you have insight?
\q1 \v 9 The one planting the ear, does he not hear?
\q1 Or the one forming the eye, does he not observe?
\q1 \v 10 The one instructing nations, does he not rebuke?
\q1 Does the one teaching mankind lack knowledge?
\q1 \v 11 Yahweh knows the thoughts of mankind,
\q1 that they are vapor.
\q1 \v 12 The joys of the man whom you instruct, Yah,
\q1 and from your law you teach him,
\q1 \v 13 to give rest to him from days of evil
\q1 until a pit is dug for the wicked.
\q1 \v 14 For Yahweh will not forsake his people
\q1 and he will not abandon his inheritance.
\q1 \v 15 For judgment will return to the right;
\q1 and all the upright in heart {are} after it.
\q1 \v 16 Who will rise up for me against the evildoers?
\q1 Who will stand up for me against the workers of wickedness?
\q1 \v 17 Unless Yahweh {had been} a help to me,
\q1 shortly my soul would have dwelt in silence.
\q1 \v 18 When I said, “My foot is slipping,”
\q1 Your covenant faithfulness, Yahweh, supported me.
\q1 \v 19 When my cares within me {are} many, your consolations gladden my soul.
\q1 \v 20 Can a throne of destruction be your ally,
\q1 one creating injustice by statute?
\q1 \v 21 They conspire together against the life of the righteous
\q1 and they condemn innocent blood.
\q1 \v 22 But Yahweh has been to me a high tower,
\q1 and my God, the rock of my refuge.
\q1 \v 23 He will return on them their iniquity
\q1 and he will destroy them in their wickedness.
\q1 Yahweh our God will destroy them.
\c 95
\q1 \v 1 Come, let us sing to Yahweh;
\q1 let us shout to the rock of our salvation!
\q1 \v 2 Let us meet his face with thanksgiving;
\q1 with psalms, let us sing joyfully to him.
\q1 \v 3 For Yahweh {is} a great God
\q1 and a great king above all gods,
\q1 \v 4 who in his hand {has} the depths of the earth;
\q1 and the heights of the mountains {are} to him,
\q1 \v 5 who to him {is} the sea, and he, he made it,
\q1 and his hands formed the dry land.
\q1 \v 6 Come, let us worship and bow down;
\q1 let us kneel to the face of Yahweh, our maker:
\q1 \v 7 For he {is} our God,
\q1 and we {are} the people of his pasture and the flock of his hand.
\q1 Today—if only you would listen to his voice!
\q1 \v 8 “Do not harden your heart, as {at} Meribah,
\q1 as {on} the day of Massah in the wilderness,
\q1 \v 9 where your fathers tested me,
\q1 tried me, though they had seen my deeds.
\q1 \v 10 For 40 years I was angry with the generation
\q1 and said, ‘They are a people wandering of heart
\q1 and they, they have not known my ways.’
\q1 \v 11 Therefore I vowed in my nose,
\q1 ‘if they enter into my rest.’”
\c 96
\q1 \v 1 Sing to Yahweh a new song;
\q1 sing to Yahweh, all the earth.
\q1 \v 2 Sing to Yahweh, bless his name;
\q1 announce his salvation from day to day.
\q1 \v 3 Recount his glory among the nations,
\q1 his marvelous deeds among all the peoples.
\q1 \v 4 For Yahweh is great and is to be praised greatly.
\q1 He is to be feared above all gods.
\q1 \v 5 For all the gods of the peoples are idols,
\q1 but Yahweh made the heavens.
\q1 \v 6 Splendor and majesty {are} to his face.
\q1 Strength and beauty {are} in his sanctuary.
\q1 \v 7 Ascribe to Yahweh, clans of peoples,
\q1 ascribe to Yahweh glory and strength.
\q1 \v 8 Give to Yahweh the glory of his name.
\q1 Bring an offering and come into his courts.
\q1 \v 9 Bow down to Yahweh in the splendor of holiness;
\q1 tremble from his face, all the earth.
\q1 \v 10 Say among the nations, “Yahweh reigns.”
\q1 Indeed, the world is established; it cannot be shaken.
\q1 He judges the peoples with evenness.
\q1 \v 11 Let the heavens be glad, and let the earth rejoice;
\q1 let the sea roar and its fullness.
\q1 \v 12 Let the fields rejoice and all that is in them.
\q1 Then let all the trees in the forest shout for joy
\q1 \v 13 to the face of Yahweh, for he is coming,
\q1 for he is coming to judge the earth.
\q1 He will judge the world with righteousness
\q1 and the peoples with his faithfulness.
\c 97
\q1 \v 1 Yahweh reigns; let the earth rejoice;
\q1 let the many coastlands be glad.
\q1 \v 2 Clouds and darkness surround him.
\q1 Righteousness and justice {are} the foundation of his throne.
\q1 \v 3 Fire goes to his face
\q1 and burns his adversaries all around.
\q1 \v 4 His lightning lights up the world;
\q1 the earth sees and trembles.
\q1 \v 5 The mountains melt like wax from to the face of Yahweh,
\q1 from to the face of the Lord of all the earth.
\q1 \v 6 The heavens declare his righteousness,
\q1 and all the peoples see his glory.
\q1 \v 7 Let all those serving a carved image have shame,
\q1 those boasting in worthless idols—
\q1 bow down to him, all you gods!
\q1 \v 8 Zion heard and was glad,
\q1 and the daughters of Judah rejoiced
\q1 because of your judgments, Yahweh.
\q1 \v 9 For you, Yahweh, are most high above all the earth.
\q1 You are exalted far above all gods.
\q1 \v 10 Lovers of Yahweh, hate evil!
\q1 The protector of the lives of his faithful,
\q1 from the hand of the wicked he snatches them.
\q1 \v 11 Light is sown for the righteous
\q1 and for the upright of heart, gladness.
\q1 \v 12 Be glad in Yahweh, you righteous;
\q1 and give thanks to the remembrance of his holiness!
\c 98
\p
\v 1 \d A psalm.
\q1 Sing to Yahweh a new song,
\q1 for he has done marvelous things;
\q1 his right hand and the arm of his holiness have brought him salvation.
\q1 \v 2 Yahweh has made known his salvation;
\q1 to the eyes of the nations he has revealed his righteousness.
\q1 \v 3 He remembers his covenant loyalty and his faithfulness to the house of Israel;
\q1 all the ends of the earth will see the salvation of our God.
\q1 \v 4 Shout to Yahweh, all the earth;
\q1 burst into song, sing for joy, and make music!
\q1 \v 5 Make music to Yahweh with the harp,
\q1 with the harp and the voice of a song.
\q1 \v 6 With trumpets and the sound of the shofar,
\q1 shout to the face of the King, Yahweh!
\q1 \v 7 Let the sea roar and its fulness,
\q1 the world and the dwellers in it!
\q1 \v 8 Let the rivers clap palm;
\q1 let the mountains rejoice together
\q1 \v 9 to the face of Yahweh who is coming to judge the earth;
\q1 he will judge the world with righteousness
\q1 and the peoples with fairness.
\c 99
\q1 \v 1 Yahweh reigns—let the peoples tremble—
\q1 sitting {above} the cherubim; let the earth quake!
\q1 \v 2 Yahweh in Zion {is} great,
\q1 and he is high above all the peoples.
\q1 \v 3 Let them praise your great and fearsome name;
\q1 holy {is} he.
\q1 \v 4 And the strength of the king: he loves justice.
\q1 You, you have established fairness;
\q1 you, you have done justice and righteousness in Jacob.
\q1 \v 5 Exalt Yahweh our God
\q1 and worship at the stool for his feet.
\q1 Holy {is} he.
\q1 \v 6 Moses and Aaron {were} among his priests,
\q1 and Samuel {was} among those calling his name.
\q1 They called to Yahweh, and he, he answered them.
\q1 \v 7 In the pillar of cloud he spoke to them.
\q1 They kept his testimonies
\q1 and the statutes he gave to them.
\q1 \v 8 Yahweh our God, you, you answered them.
\q1 A forgiving God you were to them,
\q1 but avenging concerning their deeds.
\q1 \v 9 Exalt Yahweh our God,
\q1 and worship at the hill of his holiness,
\q1 for Yahweh our God is holy.
\c 100
\p
\v 1 \d A psalm of thanksgiving.
\q1 Shout to Yahweh, all the earth.
\q1 \v 2 Serve Yahweh with gladness;
\q1 come to his face with rejoicing.
\q1 \v 3 Know that Yahweh, he {is} God;
\q1 he, he made us, and not we,
\q1 his people and the sheep of his pasture.
\q1 \v 4 Enter his gates with thanksgiving
\q1 and his courts with praise.
\q1 Give thanks to him; bless his name.
\q1 \v 5 For Yahweh {is} good; his covenant faithfulness {is} to eternity
\q1 and his truthfulness until generation and generation.
\c 101
\p
\v 1 \d A psalm of David
\q1 I shall sing {of} covenant faithfulness and justice;
\q2 to you, Yahweh, I shall sing praises.
\q1 \v 2 I shall study the blameless way.
\q1 When will you come to me?
\q1 I will walk in the integrity of my heart within my house.
\q1 \v 3 I will not put a worthless thing before my eyes;
\q1 I hate to do transgressions;
\q1 it will not cling to me.
\q1 \v 4 A perverse heart will turn away from me;
\q1 I will not know evil.
\q1 \v 5 The one slandering his neighbor in secret, him I will destroy.
\q1 The {one} lofty of eyes and the {one} wide of heart, him I cannot.
\q1 \v 6 My eyes {are} on the faithful {ones} of the land to sit with me;
\q1 The {one} walking in the way of integrity, he may serve me.
\q1 \v 7 A doer of deceit will not remain within my house;
\q1 a speaker of lies will not be established before my eyes.
\q1 \v 8 In the mornings I will destroy all the wicked of the land,
\q1 to cut off all workers of evil from the city of Yahweh.
\c 102
\d A prayer of the lowly when he is faint and pours out his meditation to the face of Yahweh.
\q1 \v 1 Hear my prayer, Yahweh;
\q1 let my cry come unto you.
\q1 \v 2 Do not hide your face from me on the day it distresses me.
\q1 Incline your ear to me.
\q1 On the day I call out, hurry, answer me.
\q1 \v 3 For my days expire like smoke,
\q1 and my bones are charred like a fireplace.
\q1 \v 4 My heart is struck like grass and withered,
\q1 for I have forgotten to eat my bread.
\q1 \v 5 From the voice of my groaning,
\q1 my bone clings to my flesh.
\q1 \v 6 I am like an owl of the wilderness;
\q1 I have become like a screech owl in the ruins.
\q1 \v 7 I am alert,
\q1 and I have become like a bird alone on a roof.
\q1 \v 8 My enemies taunt me all the day;
\q1 those mocking me swear by me.
\q1 \v 9 As ashes as bread I eat,
\q1 and I mix my drink with weeping
\q1 \v 10 from the face of your fury and rage,
\q1 for you have lifted me up and thrown me.
\q1 \v 11 My days {are} like a lengthening shadow,
\q1 and I, like grass, have withered.
\q1 \v 12 But you, Yahweh, sit forever,
\q1 and your remembrance {is} to generation and generation.
\q1 \v 13 You, you will arise, you will have mercy on Zion;
\q1 for {it is} the time to favor her;
\q1 for the appointed time has come.
\q1 \v 14 For your servants cherish her stones
\q1 and favor her dust.
\q1 \v 15 The nations will fear the name of Yahweh,
\q1 and all the kings of the earth, your glory.
\q1 \v 16 For Yahweh builds Zion;
\q1 he appears in his glory.
\q1 \v 17 He turns to the prayer of the destitute
\q1 and he does not despise their prayer.
\q1 \v 18 This will be written for a future generation,
\q1 and a people being created will praise Yah;
\q1 \v 19 that he looked down from the height of his holiness;
\q1 Yahweh from heaven regarded the earth,
\q1 \v 20 to hear the groaning of the prisoner,
\q1 to release the sons of execution.
\q1 \v 21 To recount the name of Yahweh in Zion
\q1 and his praise in Jerusalem
\q1 \v 22 when peoples and kingdoms gather together
\q1 to serve Yahweh.
\q1 \v 23 He has broken my strength on the road.
\q1 He has shortened my days.
\q1 \v 24 I said, “My God, do not take me away in the middle of my days;
\q1 your years {are} a generation of generations.
\q1 \v 25 Formerly you set the earth,
\q1 and the heavens {are} the work of your hands.
\q1 \v 26 They, they will perish, but you, you will stand,
\q1 and all of them will wear out like a garment;
\q1 like clothing, you will pass them off, and they will pass away.
\q1 \v 27 But you {are} he,
\q1 and your years will not end.
\q1 \v 28 The sons of your servants will abide,
\q1 and their seed will be established to your face.”
\c 103
\q1 \v 1 \d Of David
\q1 Bless Yahweh, my soul!
\q1 And all of my inward parts, the name of his holiness.
\q1 \v 2 Bless Yahweh, my soul!
\q1 And do not forget all of his benefits.
\q1 \v 3 The one pardoning all your sins;
\q1 the one healing all your diseases.
\q1 \v 4 The one redeeming your life from the pit;
\q1 the one crowning you with covenant faithfulness and mercy.
\q1 \v 5 The one satisfying your ornaments with good;
\q1 your youth renews itself like the eagle.
\q1 \v 6 Yahweh, doing righteousness and justice for all those being oppressed.
\q1 \v 7 He made known his ways to Moses,
\q1 his deeds to the children of Israel.
\q1 \v 8 Yahweh {is} merciful and gracious,
\q1 long of nostrils and abundant in covenant faithfulness.
\q1 \v 9 He will not contend to the end,
\q1 and he will not maintain forever.
\q1 \v 10 He does not deal with us according to our sins,
\q1 and he does not treat us according to our iniquities.
\q1 \v 11 For as the heavens are high above the earth,
\q1 his covenant faithfulness is strong toward those fearing him.
\q1 \v 12 As far as the sunrise {is} from the sunset,
\q1 he has removed our transgressions from us.
\q1 \v 13 As a father has compassion on his children,
\q1 Yahweh has compassion on those fearing him.
\q1 \v 14 For he, he knows our form;
\q1 remembering that we {are} dust.
\q1 \v 15 A man, his days {are} like grass;
\q1 like a flower of the field, thus he flourishes.
\q1 \v 16 For the wind passes over it, and it is no more,
\q1 and its place does not acknowledge it again.
\q1 \v 17 But the covenant faithfulness of Yahweh {is} from everlasting to everlasting on those fearing him,
\q1 and his righteousness {is} to the children of children,
\q1 \v 18 to the ones keeping his covenant,
\q1 and to the ones remembering his precepts, to do them.
\q1 \v 19 Yahweh has established his throne in the heavens,
\q1 and his kingdom rules over all.
\q1 \v 20 Bless Yahweh, his angels,
\q1 warriors of strength, doers of his word,
\q1 listening to the voice of his word!
\q1 \v 21 Bless Yahweh, all his hosts,
\q1 ministering to him, doing his pleasure!
\q1 \v 22 Bless Yahweh, all his works,
\q1 in all the places of his reign!
\q1 Bless Yahweh, my soul!
\c 104
\q1 \v 1 Bless Yahweh, my soul!
\q1 Yahweh my God, you are very great;
\q1 you are clothed with splendor and majesty,
\q1 \v 2 wrapping light as the garment;
\q1 spreading out the heavens as the tent curtain;
\q1 \v 3 the one setting his upper chambers on the waters;
\q1 the one appointing the clouds his chariot;
\q1 the one walking on the wings of the wind;
\q1 \v 4 making the winds his messengers,
\q1 flaming fire, his servants.
\q1 \v 5 He set the earth upon its foundations;
\q1 it will not be moved forever and ever.
\q1 \v 6 You covered it {with} the deep like a garment;
\q1 the waters stood above the mountains.
\q1 \v 7 From your rebuke they fled;
\q1 from your voice of thunder they hurried away.
\q1 \v 8 They ascended the mountains; they descended the valleys,
\q1 to the place that you had appointed for them.
\q1 \v 9 You set a boundary they cannot pass;
\q1 they will not return to cover the earth.
\q1 \v 10 The one sending springs into the wadis—
\q1 between the mountains they flow.
\q1 \v 11 They give drink to all his animals of the field;
\q1 the wild donkeys break their thirst.
\q1 \v 12 Alongside them the birds of the heavens dwell;
\q1 from between the branches they give voice.
\q1 \v 13 The one watering the mountains from his upper chambers—
\q1 from the fruit of your works the earth is satisfied.
\q1 \v 14 The one making grass grow for the cattle
\q1 and plants for the work of man
\q1 to bring forth bread from the earth.
\q1 \v 15 And wine—he gladdens the heart of man,
\q1 to make the face shine from oil,
\q1 and bread—he sustains the heart of man.
\q1 \v 16 The trees of Yahweh are satisfied—
\q1 the cedars of Lebanon which he planted,
\q1 \v 17 where birds make their nests there,
\q1 the stork, the cypress tree her home,
\q1 \v 18 the high mountains for the wild goats,
\q1 the cliffs, a refuge for the hyraxes.
\q1 \v 19 He made the moon for appointed times;
\q1 the sun knows its setting.
\q1 \v 20 You set darkness and it is night;
\q1 in it all of his creatures of the forest crawl—
\q1 \v 21 the young lions roaring for prey
\q1 and seeking their food from God.
\q1 \v 22 The sun rises, they retreat,
\q1 and lie down in their dens.
\q1 \v 23 Man goes out to his work
\q1 and to his labor until evening.
\q1 \v 24 How many {are} your works, Yahweh!
\q1 You made all of them with wisdom;
\q1 the earth is full of your creation.
\q1 \v 25 There {is} the sea, great and broad of hands;
\q1 creeping things {are} there,
\q1 and there is no number,
\q1 living things, small with great.
\q1 \v 26 Ships travel there;
\q1 Leviathan, which you formed to play in it.
\q1 \v 27 All of them look to you to give
\q1 their food at its time.
\q1 \v 28 You give to them; they gather {it};
\q1 you open your hand; they are satisfied {with} good.
\q1 \v 29 You hide your face; they are terrified;
\q1 you take away their breath; they expire
\q1 and return to their dust.
\q1 \v 30 You send out your breath; they are created,
\q1 and you renew the face of the land.
\q1 \v 31 May the glory of Yahweh be forever;
\q1 may Yahweh rejoice in his creation!
\q1 \v 32 The one looking at the earth, and it shakes—
\q1 he touches the mountains, and they smoke.
\q1 \v 33 I shall sing to Yahweh in my life;
\q1 I shall sing praise to my God during my existence.
\q1 \v 34 May my meditation be sweet to him;
\q1 I, I will rejoice in Yahweh.
\q1 \v 35 May sinners cease from the earth,
\q1 and the wicked be no more.
\q1 Bless Yahweh, my soul!
\q1 Hallelu Yah!
\c 105
\q1 \v 1 Give thanks to Yahweh, call on his name;
\q1 make known his deeds among the peoples!
\q1 \v 2 Sing to him, make music to him;
\q1 exclaim about all of his marvelous deeds!
\q1 \v 3 Boast in the name of his holiness;
\q1 let the heart of the seekers of Yahweh rejoice.
\q1 \v 4 Seek Yahweh and his strength;
\q1 search for his face continually.
\q1 \v 5 Recall the marvelous things that he has done,
\q1 his miracles and the decrees from his mouth,
\q1 \v 6 seed of Abraham his servant,
\q1 sons of Jacob, his chosen ones.
\q1 \v 7 He is Yahweh, our God.
\q1 His decrees {are} in all the earth.
\q1 \v 8 He remembers his covenant forever,
\q1 the word he commanded for a thousand generations,
\q1 \v 9 that he cut with Abraham
\q1 and his oath to Isaac.
\q1 \v 10 He confirmed it to Jacob as a statute;
\q1 to Israel, an everlasting covenant,
\q1 \v 11 saying, “I will give to you the land of Canaan
\q1 {as} the portion of your inheritance,”
\q1 \v 12 when they were few in number,
\q1 very few, and strangers in it.
\q1 \v 13 They wandered from nation to nation,
\q1 from a kingdom to other people.
\q1 \v 14 He did not allow anyone to oppress them;
\q1 he rebuked kings because of them.
\q1 \v 15 “Do not touch my anointed ones,
\q1 and do not harm my prophets.”
\q1 \v 16 He called for a famine on the land;
\q1 he broke all of the staff of bread.
\q1 \v 17 He sent a man ahead of them;
\q1 Joseph was sold as a servant.
\q1 \v 18 They oppressed his feet in a shackle;
\q1 his neck went into the iron,
\q1 \v 19 until the time of his word coming to pass.
\q1 The speaking of Yahweh refined him.
\q1 \v 20 The king sent and released him;
\q1 the one ruling the people, and liberated him.
\q1 \v 21 He appointed him lord of his house
\q1 and ruler over all of his possessions
\q1 \v 22 to bind his princes according to his soul
\q1 and he taught his elders wisdom.
\q1 \v 23 Then Israel came into Egypt,
\q1 and Jacob sojourned in the land of Ham.
\q1 \v 24 He made his people very fruitful,
\q1 and he made him stronger than his enemies.
\q1 \v 25 He turned their hearts to hate his people,
\q1 to plot against his servants.
\q1 \v 26 He sent Moses, his servant,
\q1 Aaron, whom he had chosen him.
\q1 \v 27 They performed among them the matters of his signs,
\q1 and his wonders in the land of Ham.
\q1 \v 28 He sent darkness and made it dark,
\q1 and they did not rebel against his words.
\q1 \v 29 He turned their water into blood
\q1 and killed their fish.
\q1 \v 30 Their land swarmed with frogs—
\q1 in the rooms of their kings!
\q1 \v 31 He spoke, and flies came;
\q1 gnats in all their territory.
\q1 \v 32 He made their rain hail,
\q1 fire of flames on their land.
\q1 \v 33 He struck their vines and their figs;
\q1 he shattered the trees of their territory.
\q1 \v 34 He spoke, and the locust came,
\q1 and the young locust, and there was no number.
\q1 \v 35 And they ate all of the vegetation in their land;
\q1 and they ate the fruit of their ground.
\q1 \v 36 Then he struck every firstborn in their land,
\q1 the first of all their strength.
\q1 \v 37 He brought them out with silver and gold;
\q1 and there was no stumbling among his tribes.
\q1 \v 38 Egypt was glad when they departed,
\q1 for the dread of them had fallen upon them.
\q1 \v 39 He spread a cloud for a covering
\q1 and fire to light up the night.
\q1 \v 40 He asked, and he brought quail
\q1 and satisfied them with bread from heaven.
\q1 \v 41 He split the rock and waters gushed out;
\q1 they went forth in the desert a river.
\q1 \v 42 For he remembered the word of his holiness
\q1 with Abraham his servant.
\q1 \v 43 He led his people out with joy,
\q1 his chosen with shouts of triumph.
\q1 \v 44 Then he gave to them the lands of the nations,
\q1 and they took possession of the toil of the peoples
\q1 \v 45 so that they might keep his statutes
\q1 and comply with his laws.
\q1 Hallelu Yah!
\c 106
\q1 \v 1 Hallelu Yah!
\q1 Give thanks to Yahweh, for {he is} good,
\q1 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 2 Who can utter the mighty acts of Yahweh,
\q1 proclaim all of his praise?
\q1 \v 3 The happinesses of the guardians of justice,
\q1 the doers of righteousness at all times!
\q1 \v 4 Remember me, Yahweh, in the favor of your people;
\q1 visit me in your salvation,
\q1 \v 5 to look on the good of your chosen,
\q1 to rejoice in the gladness of your nation,
\q1 to boast with your inheritance.
\q1 \v 6 We have sinned like our fathers;
\q1 we have done wrong; we have done evil.
\q1 \v 7 Our fathers did not consider your marvelous deeds in Egypt;
\q1 they did not remember the abundance of your covenant faithfulness,
\q1 and they rebelled at the sea, the Sea of Reeds.
\q1 \v 8 But he saved them on account of his name,
\q1 to make known his power.
\q1 \v 9 He rebuked the Sea of Reeds, and it dried up.
\q1 Then he led them through the depths, as {through} a desert.
\q1 \v 10 So he saved them from the hand of the hater,
\q1 and he rescued them from the hand of the enemy.
\q1 \v 11 Then the waters covered their adversaries;
\q1 one of them was not left.
\q1 \v 12 Then they believed his words;
\q1 they sang his praise.
\q1 \v 13 But they hurried, they forgot his deeds;
\q1 they did not wait for his instructions.
\q1 \v 14 And they craved a craving in the wilderness,
\q1 and they tested God in the wasteland.
\q1 \v 15 So he gave to them their request,
\q2 but he sent a wasting disease upon their lives.
\q1 \v 16 And they became envious of Moses in the camp,
\q1 of Aaron, the holy one of Yahweh.
\q1 \v 17 The earth opened and swallowed Dathan
\q1 and covered over the congregation of Abiram.
\q1 \v 18 Fire blazed up in their congregation;
\q1 a flame burned up the wicked.
\q1 \v 19 They made a calf at Horeb
\q1 and worshiped a cast image.
\q1 \v 20 Thus they traded their Glory
\q1 for the likeness of a bull eating grass.
\q1 \v 21 They forgot God their Savior,
\q1 the doer of great {deeds} in Egypt:
\q1 \v 22 wonders in the land of Ham,
\q1 awesome {acts} at the Sea of Reeds.
\q1 \v 23 So he said to annihilate them—
\q1 had not Moses, his chosen one, stood in the breach to his face,
\q1 to turn away his heat from destroying.
\q1 \v 24 Then they despised the delightful land;
\q1 they did not believe his word,
\q1 \v 25 but grumbled in their tents;
\q1 they did not listen to the voice of Yahweh.
\q1 \v 26 Then he raised his hand to them
\q1 to make them fall in the desert,
\q1 \v 27 and to make their seed fall among the nations,
\q1 and to scatter them among the lands.
\q1 \v 28 They joined themselves to the Baal of Peor
\q1 and ate the sacrifices of the dead.
\q1 \v 29 And they angered with their actions,
\q1 and a plague broke out among them.
\q1 \v 30 Then Phinehas stood and intervened,
\q1 and the plague was restrained.
\q1 \v 31 It was counted to him as righteousness
\q1 to generation and generation until forever.
\q1 \v 32 And they angered at the waters of Meribah,
\q1 and it was bad for Moses on account of them.
\q1 \v 33 For they rebelled against his spirit,
\q1 and he spoke rashly with his lips.
\q1 \v 34 They did not destroy the peoples,
\q1 which Yahweh had said to them,
\q1 \v 35 but they mingled with the nations
\q1 and learned their ways
\q1 \v 36 and served their idols,
\q1 and they became a snare to them.
\q1 \v 37 And they sacrificed their sons and their daughters to demons.
\q1 \v 38 And they shed innocent blood,
\q1 the blood of their sons and their daughters,
\q1 whom they sacrificed to the idols of Canaan,
\q1 and the land was desecrated by bloodshed.
\q1 \v 39 And they became unclean by their deeds;
\q1 and they prostituted themselves by their actions.
\q1 \v 40 So Yahweh’s nose burned with his people,
\q1 and he despised his inheritance.
\q1 \v 41 And he gave them into the hand of the nations,
\q1 and the haters of them ruled over them.
\q1 \v 42 And their enemies oppressed them,
\q1 and they were humbled under their hand.
\q1 \v 43 Many times he rescued them,
\q1 but they, they were rebellious in their counsel
\q1 and sank in their sin.
\q1 \v 44 Yet he saw in the narrow to them,
\q1 when he was hearing their cry.
\q1 \v 45 And he remembered his covenant with them
\q1 and relented because of the abundance of his covenant faithfulness.
\q1 \v 46 He gave them for compassion to the face of all of their captors.
\q1 \v 47 Save us, Yahweh, our God!
\q1 Gather us from the nations
\q1 to give thanks to the name of your holiness,
\q1 to glory in your praises.
\q1 \v 48 May Yahweh, the God of Israel, be blessed
\q1 from everlasting and to everlasting,
\q1 and all the people say, “Amen.
\q1 Hallelu Yah!”
\c 107
\ms1 Book Five
\q1 \v 1 Give thanks to Yahweh, for {he is} good,
\q1 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 2 Let the redeemed of Yahweh say {it},
\q1 who he rescued them from the hand of the opponent.
\q1 \v 3 And he has gathered them from lands,
\q1 from the sunrise and from the evening,
\q1 from the north and from the sea.
\q1 \v 4 They wandered in the desert with wilderness for a road;
\q1 a city for a home they did not find.
\q1 \v 5 Hungry and thirsty,
\q1 their soul fainted within them.
\q1 \v 6 Then they called out to Yahweh in the distressing to them;
\q1 he rescued them from their distresses.
\q1 \v 7 He led them by a direct path
\q1 to go to a city of dwelling.
\q1 \v 8 May they thank Yahweh {for} his covenant faithfulness
\q1 and his amazing deeds for the sons of man!
\q1 \v 9 For he satisfies the thirsty soul,
\q1 and the hungry soul he fills with good.
\q1 \v 10 Sitting in darkness and gloom,
\q1 prisoners of affliction and iron
\q1 \v 11 because they had rebelled against the words of God
\q1 and despised the counsel of the Most High,
\q1 \v 12 he humbled their hearts through hardship;
\q1 they stumbled and there was no helper.
\q1 \v 13 Then they cried out to Yahweh in the distressing to them;
\q1 he saved them from their distresses.
\q1 \v 14 He brought them out of darkness and gloom
\q1 and broke apart their bonds.
\q1 \v 15 May they thank Yahweh {for} his covenant faithfulness
\q1 and his amazing deeds for the sons of man!
\q1 \v 16 For he has broken the gates of bronze
\q1 and cut through the bars of iron.
\q1 \v 17 Foolish from their rebellious way
\q1 and afflicted from their sins,
\q1 \v 18 their soul detested all food,
\q1 and they touched the gates of death.
\q1 \v 19 Then they cried out to Yahweh in the distressing to them;
\q1 he saved them from their distresses.
\q1 \v 20 He sent his word and healed them,
\q1 and he delivered them from their destruction.
\q1 \v 21 May they thank Yahweh {for} his covenant faithfulness
\q1 and his amazing deeds for the sons of man!
\q1 \v 22 May they sacrifice sacrifices of thanksgiving
\q1 and recount his deeds with a shout!
\q1 \v 23 Going down to the sea in ships,
\q1 doing business on abundant waters,
\q1 \v 24 they, they saw the deeds of Yahweh
\q1 and his wonders in the deep.
\q1 \v 25 Then he spoke and aroused the wind of a hurricane
\q1 and raised up his waves.
\q1 \v 26 They went up {to} the sky; they went down {to} the depths.
\q1 Their souls melted in the disaster.
\q1 \v 27 They swayed and staggered as intoxicated
\q1 and all their wisdom became confounded.
\q1 \v 28 Then they cried out to Yahweh in the distressing to them
\q1 and he rescued them from their distresses.
\q1 \v 29 He raised the storm to calmness
\q1 and he quieted the waves.
\q1 \v 30 Then they rejoiced because they subsided,
\q1 and he guided them to the harbor of their desire.
\q1 \v 31 May they thank Yahweh {for} his covenant faithfulness
\q1 and his amazing deeds for the sons of man!
\q1 \v 32 May they exalt him in the assembly of the people
\q1 and praise him at the seat of the elders.
\q1 \v 33 He turns rivers into a desert
\q1 and springs of water into thirsty land,
\q1 \v 34 fruitful ground into salt land,
\q1 from the wickedness of the dwellers in it.
\q1 \v 35 He turns the wilderness into a pool of water
\q1 and dry land into springs of water.
\q1 \v 36 He settles the hungry there,
\q2 and they build a city of dwelling.
\q1 \v 37 Then they sow fields and plant vineyards,
\q1 and they produce the fruit of the harvest.
\q1 \v 38 He blesses them and they become very many
\q1 and their cattle do not become few.
\q1 \v 39 Then they become few and become low
\q1 from distress of evil and sorrow.
\q1 \v 40 He pours contempt on the leaders
\q1 and causes them to wander in an empty place of no road.
\q1 \v 41 But he raises up the needy from affliction
\q1 and establishes families like a flock.
\q1 \v 42 The upright see and rejoice,
\q1 and all wickedness shuts its mouth.
\q1 \v 43 Who is wise? Then may he keep these things
\q1 and may they ponder the covenant faithfulness of Yahweh.
\c 108
\d A song; a psalm of David.
\q1 \v 1 My heart is made steadfast, God;
\q2 I will sing and I will make music, indeed, {with} my glory!
\q1 \v 2 Awaken, lyre and harp;
\q2 I will awaken the dawn.
\q1 \v 3 I will thank you, Yahweh, among the peoples;
\q2 I will make music to you among the nations.
\q1 \v 4 For your covenant faithfulness {is} great from above the heavens,
\q2 and your trustworthiness, above the clouds.
\q1 \v 5 Be exalted, God, above the heavens,
\q2 and your glory, over all the earth.
\q1 \v 6 So that your beloved ones may be rescued,
\q2 save {with} your right hand and answer me.
\q1 \v 7 God has spoken in his holiness: “I shall rejoice;
\q2 I shall divide Shechem and measure out the Valley of Succoth.
\q1 \v 8 To me {is} Gilead; to me {is} Manasseh,
\q2 and Ephraim {is} the protection of my head,
\q2 Judah, my scepter.
\q1 \v 9 Moab {is} a tub for my washing;
\q2 over Edom I throw my sandal;
\q2 over Philistia I shout triumphantly.”
\q1 \v 10 Who will bring me {into} the strong city?
\q2 Who will lead me to Edom?
\q1 \v 11 God, have you not rejected us?
\q2 And you do not go out with our army, God.
\q1 \v 12 Give to us help against the enemy,
\q2 and futility {is} the deliverance of man.
\q1 \v 13 With God we will accomplish valor;
\q2 and he, he will trample our adversaries.
\c 109
\p
\v 1 \d To the chief musician: a psalm of David.
\q1 God of my praise, do not be silent!
\q1 \v 2 For a wicked mouth and a mouth of deceit open against me;
\q2 they speak a tongue of untruth with me,
\q1 \v 3 and words of hatred surround me,
\q2 and they attack me without cause.
\q1 \v 4 In return for my love they accuse me,
\q2 but I—prayer.
\q1 \v 5 They put upon me evil in return for good,
\q2 and hatred in return for my love.
\q1 \v 6 Appoint a wicked one over him;
\q2 and may an accuser stand at his right hand.
\q1 \v 7 When he is judged, may he come out guilty;
\q2 and may his prayer be as sin.
\q1 \v 8 May his days be few;
\q2 may another take his position.
\q1 \v 9 May his children be fatherless,
\q2 and his wife a widow.
\q1 \v 10 And wandering, may his children wander and beg
\q2 and seek from their desolations.
\q1 \v 11 May a creditor snare all that {is} to him;
\q2 may strangers plunder his work.
\q1 \v 12 May there not be to him {one} extending covenant faithfulness;
\q2 and may there not be {one} pitying his orphans.
\q1 \v 13 May his posterity be to cut off;
\q2 may their name be blotted out in the next generation.
\q1 \v 14 May the sin of his fathers be remembered to Yahweh;
\q2 and the offense of his mother not be blotted out.
\q1 \v 15 May they be before Yahweh continually
\q2 and may he cut off their remembrance from the earth,
\q1 \v 16 because he never remembered to do covenant faithfulness,
\q2 but pursued the humble man and the needy
\q2 and the dejected in heart to death.
\q1 \v 17 And he loved cursing, and it came to him,
\q2 and he did not delight in blessing, and it was far from him.
\q1 \v 18 And he put on cursing as his garment,
\q2 and it entered into his inner being like water,
\q2 and like oil into his bones.
\q1 \v 19 May it be to him like the clothing he wears,
\q2 and for the belt he always girds himself with it.
\q1 \v 20 This, the payment of my accusers from Yahweh,
\q2 and those speaking evil against my soul.
\q1 \v 21 But you, Yahweh, my Lord, do with me on account of your name.
\q2 Because your covenant faithfulness {is} good, rescue me!
\q1 \v 22 For I am poor and needy,
\q2 and my heart breaks within me.
\q1 \v 23 Like a shadow when it lengthens I am made to go;
\q2 I am shaken off like a locust.
\q1 \v 24 My knees are weak from fasting
\q2 and my flesh is gaunt from fatness.
\q1 \v 25 And I, I am a disgrace to them;
\q2 they see me; they shake their head.
\q1 \v 26 Help me, Yahweh my God;
\q2 save me according to your covenant faithfulness,
\q1 \v 27 so that they know that this {is} your hand;
\q2 you, Yahweh, you have done it.
\q1 \v 28 They, they will curse, but you, you will bless;
\q2 they arise, but then become ashamed,
\q2 and your servant will rejoice.
\q1 \v 29 May my accusers be clothed with disgrace;
\q2 may they wear their shame like a robe.
\q1 \v 30 With my mouth I greatly thank Yahweh;
\q2 and in the midst of many I will praise him.
\q1 \v 31 For he stands at the right hand of the needy,
\q2 to save {him} from the judges of his soul.
\c 110
\p
\v 1 \d Of David, a psalm.
\q1 The declaration of Yahweh to my lord {the king}:
\q1 “Sit at my right hand
\q2 until I make your enemies a footstool for your feet.”
\q1 \v 2 Yahweh will stretch out the scepter of your strength from Zion;
\q2 rule in the midst of your enemies!
\q1 \v 3 Your people, freewill offerings on the day of your strength, in the beauty of holiness;
\q2 from the womb of the dawn, the dew of your youth {is} to you.
\q1 \v 4 Yahweh has sworn, and will not revoke {it}:
\q1 “You {are} a priest forever,
\q2 after the manner of Melchizedek.”
\q1 \v 5 The Lord {is} at your right hand.
\q2 He crushes kings on the day of his nose.
\q1 \v 6 He will judge the nations;
\q2 he fills {with} bodies, he crushes the head,
\q2 upon abundant land.
\q1 \v 7 He will drink from the stream along the path,
\q2 Therefore, he will lift up the head.
\c 111
\q1 \v 1 Hallelu Yah!
\q1 I will thank Yahweh with the whole heart
\q2 in the assembly of the upright and congregation.
\q1 \v 2 The works of Yahweh {are} great,
\q2 searched by everyone desirous of them.
\q1 \v 3 His work {is} splendor and majesty,
\q2 and his righteousness stands forever.
\q1 \v 4 He makes a remembrance for his wonders;
\q2 Yahweh {is} gracious and merciful.
\q1 \v 5 He gives food to those fearing him.
\q2 He remembers his covenant forever.
\q1 \v 6 He showed the power of his works to his people,
\q2 to give to them the inheritance of the nations.
\q1 \v 7 The works of his hands {are} truth and justice;
\q2 all of his precepts are reliable.
\q1 \v 8 They are established forever, for eternity,
\q2 done in faithfulness, and upright.
\q1 \v 9 He has sent redemption to his people;
\q2 he ordained his covenant forever;
\q2 holy and awesome {is} his name.
\q1 \v 10 The fear of Yahweh {is} the beginning of wisdom;
\q2 good understanding to all those doing them.
\q2 His praise stands forever!
\c 112
\q1 \v 1 Hallelu Yah!
\q1 The happinesses of the man fearing Yahweh,
\q2 greatly delighting in his commandments!
\q1 \v 2 His seed will be powerful on the earth;
\q2 a generation of upright ones will be blessed.
\q1 \v 3 Wealth and riches {are} in his house,
\q2 and his righteousness stands forever.
\q1 \v 4 Light shines in the darkness for the upright ones;
\q1 gracious and compassionate and just.
\q1 \v 5 a gracious and lending man {is} good;
\q1 he conducts his affairs with justice.
\q1 \v 6 For he will not be moved for forever;
\q1 the righteous will be for an eternal remembrance.
\q1 \v 7 He does not fear bad news;
\q1 his heart is sure, trusting in Yahweh.
\q1 \v 8 His heart is upheld, he does not fear,
\q1 until he looks over his adversaries.
\q1 \v 9 He scatters, he gives to the poor;
\q1 his righteousness stands forever;
\q1 his horn is high with honor.
\q1 \v 10 The wicked will see and be angry;
\q1 he will grind his teeth and he will melt away;
\q1 the desire of the wicked will perish.
\c 113
\q1 \v 1 Hallelu Yah!
\q1 Praise him, servants of Yahweh;
\q1 praise the name of Yahweh!
\q1 \v 2 Blessed be the name of Yahweh,
\q1 from now and to forever.
\q1 \v 3 From the rising of the sun to its setting,
\q1 may the name of Yahweh be praised.
\q1 \v 4 Yahweh is high above all nations;
\q1 his glory above the skies.
\q1 \v 5 Who is like Yahweh our God,
\q1 the one making high to sit,
\q1 \v 6 the one making low to look
\q1 on the sky and on the earth?
\q1 \v 7 raising up the poor from the dust,
\q1 he lifts the needy from the garbage,
\q1 \v 8 to seat him with princes,
\q1 with the princes of his people.
\q1 \v 9 He causes the barren woman of the house to dwell,
\q1 the joyful mother of children!
\q1 Hallelu Yah!
\c 114
\q1 \v 1 When Israel went out from Egypt,
\q2 the house of Jacob from a people speaking a foreign language,
\q1 \v 2 Judah became his sanctuary,
\q2 Israel his realm.
\q1 \v 3 The sea looked and fled;
\q2 the Jordan turned backward.
\q1 \v 4 The mountains skipped like rams,
\q2 the hills like sons of the flock.
\q1 \v 5 What {is} to you, sea, that you flee?
\q2 Jordan, you turn backwards?
\q1 \v 6 Mountains, you skip like rams,
\q2 hills, like sons of the flock?
\q1 \v 7 Tremble, earth, from to the face of the Lord,
\q2 from to the face of the God of Jacob,
\q1 \v 8 the one turning the rock into a pool of water,
\q2 flint into a spring of water!
\c 115
\q1 \v 1 Not to us, Yahweh, not to us,
\q1 but to your name give honor,
\q1 upon your covenant faithfulness, upon your trustworthiness.
\q1 \v 2 Why should the nations say,
\q1 “Where, then, {is} their God?”
\q1 \v 3 And our God {is} in heaven;
\q1 everything that he desires, he does.
\q1 \v 4 Their idols {are} silver and gold,
\q1 the work of the hands of man.
\q1 \v 5 A mouth {is} to them, but they do not speak;
\q1 eyes {are} to them, but they do not see;
\q1 \v 6 ears {are} to them, but they do not hear;
\q1 a nose {is} to them, but they do not smell.
\q1 \v 7 Their hands, but they do not feel;
\q1 their feet, but they cannot walk;
\q1 they do not murmur in their throats.
\q1 \v 8 Their makers are like them—
\q1 everyone who is trusting in them.
\q1 \v 9 Israel, trust in Yahweh;
\q1 he {is} their help and their shield.
\q1 \v 10 House of Aaron, trust in Yahweh;
\q1 he {is} their help and their shield.
\q1 \v 11 Fearers of Yahweh, trust in Yahweh;
\q2 he {is} their help and their shield.
\q1 \v 12 Yahweh remembers us; he will bless;
\q1 he will bless the house of Israel;
\q1 he will bless the house of Aaron.
\q1 \v 13 He will bless those fearing Yahweh,
\q1 the small with the great.
\q1 \v 14 May Yahweh add to you,
\q1 to you and to your sons.
\q1 \v 15 May you be blessed by Yahweh,
\q1 the maker of heaven and earth.
\q1 \v 16 The heavens of heavens {are} to Yahweh;
\q1 but the earth he has given to the sons of man.
\q1 \v 17 The dead do not praise Yah,
\q1 and not any descending {to} silence;
\q1 \v 18 But we, we will bless Yah
\q1 from now and to forever!
\q1 Hallelu Yah!
\c 116
\q1 \v 1 I love {him} because Yahweh hears
\q1 my voice, my pleas,
\q1 \v 2 because he extends his ear to me;
\q1 and throughout my days I will call out.
\q1 \v 3 The cords of death surrounded me,
\q1 and the constrictions of Sheol found me;
\q1 I found anguish and sorrow.
\q1 \v 4 Then I called on the name of Yahweh:
\q1 “Please Yahweh, rescue my life.”
\q1 \v 5 Yahweh {is} merciful and righteous,
\q1 and our God {is} compassionate.
\q1 \v 6 Yahweh guards the naive;
\q1 I was low, and he saved me.
\q1 \v 7 Return to your rest, my soul,
\q1 for Yahweh has repaid you.
\q1 \v 8 For you rescued my soul from death,
\q1 my eye from weeping,
\q1 my foot from stumbling.
\q1 \v 9 I will walk to the face of Yahweh
\q1 in the lands of the living.
\q1 \v 10 I trusted, though I spoke,
\q1 “I, I am very wretched.”
\q1 \v 11 I, I said in my panic,
\q1 “All mankind lies.”
\q1 \v 12 How can I return to Yahweh
\q1 all of his bestowments to me?
\q1 \v 13 I will raise the cup of salvation,
\q1 and call on the name of Yahweh.
\q1 \v 14 I will fulfill my vows to Yahweh
\q1 right in front of all of his people.
\q1 \v 15 Precious in the eyes of Yahweh
\q1 {is} the death of his faithful.
\q1 \v 16 Indeed, Yahweh, for I {am} your servant;
\q1 I {am} your servant, the son of your servant woman;
\q1 you have undone my bonds.
\q1 \v 17 I will sacrifice to you the sacrifice of thanksgiving
\q1 and I will call on the name of Yahweh.
\q1 \v 18 I will fulfill my vows to Yahweh
\q1 right in front of all of his people,
\q1 \v 19 in the courts of the house of Yahweh,
\q1 in your midst, Jerusalem.
\q1 Hallelu Yah!
\c 117
\q1 \v 1 Praise Yahweh, all nations;
\q1 extol him, all peoples!
\q1 \v 2 For his covenant faithfulness is strong toward us,
\q1 and the trustworthiness of Yahweh {is} to forever.
\q1 Hallelu Yah!
\c 118
\q1 \v 1 Give thanks to Yahweh, for {he is} good,
\q1 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever!
\q1 \v 2 Let Israel indeed say,
\q1 “For his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.”
\q1 \v 3 Let the house of Aaron indeed say,
\q1 “For his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.”
\q1 \v 4 Let the fearers of Yahweh indeed say,
\q1 “For his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.”
\q1 \v 5 From the constriction I called out to Yah;
\q1 Yah answered me with wideness.
\q1 \v 6 Yahweh {is} for me; I will not be afraid;
\q1 what can man do to me?
\q1 \v 7 Yahweh {is} for me as my helper,
\q1 and I, I will gaze on the haters of me.
\q1 \v 8 Better to take shelter in Yahweh
\q1 than to trust in man.
\q1 \v 9 Better to take shelter in Yahweh
\q1 than to trust in princes.
\q1 \v 10 All the nations surrounded me;
\q1 in the name of Yahweh, indeed I fended them off.
\q1 \v 11 They surrounded me; yes, they surrounded me;
\q1 in the name of Yahweh, indeed I fended them off.
\q1 \v 12 They surrounded me like bees;
\q1 they were extinguished like a fire of thorns;
\q1 in the name of Yahweh, indeed I fended them off.
\q1 \v 13 To push down, you pushed me down to fall,
\q1 but Yahweh helped me.
\q1 \v 14 Yah {is} my strength and song,
\q1 and he is to me for salvation.
\q1 \v 15 The voice of a shout and salvation {is} in the tents of the righteous;
\q1 the right hand of Yahweh does valor!
\q1 \v 16 The right hand of Yahweh is high;
\q1 the right hand of Yahweh does valor!
\q1 \v 17 I will not die, but live
\q1 and I will declare the deeds of Yah.
\q1 \v 18 To chastise, Yah has chastised me;
\q1 but to death he has not given me.
\q1 \v 19 Open to me the gates of righteousness;
\q1 I will enter them; I will thank Yah.
\q1 \v 20 This {is} the gate of Yahweh;
\q1 the righteous may enter through it.
\q1 \v 21 I will thank you, for you answered me,
\q1 and you have become salvation for me.
\q1 \v 22 The stone that the builders rejected
\q1 has become the head of the corner.
\q1 \v 23 This is from Yahweh;
\q1 it is marvelous in our eyes.
\q1 \v 24 This {is} the day Yahweh made;
\q1 Let us rejoice and be glad in it.
\q1 \v 25 Please, Yahweh, save please!
\q1 Please, Yahweh, give success please!
\q1 \v 26 Blessed is the one coming in the name of Yahweh;
\q1 we bless you from the house of Yahweh.
\q1 \v 27 Yahweh {is} God, and he has given light to us;
\q1 bind the sacrifice with cords to the horns of the altar.
\q1 \v 28 You {are} my God, and I will thank you;
\q1 my God, I will exalt you.
\q1 \v 29 Give thanks to Yahweh; for {he is} good;
\q1 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever!
\c 119
\qa ALEPH
\q1 \v 1 The happinesses of the blameless of way,
\q1 the ones walking in the teaching of Yahweh!
\q1 \v 2 The happinesses of the keepers of his testimonies!
\q1 They seek him with a whole heart.
\q1 \v 3 Surely they do not practice injustice;
\q1 they walk in his ways.
\q1 \v 4 You, you have commanded your precepts
\q1 to keep diligently.
\q1 \v 5 Oh, that my paths would be established
\q1 to keep your statutes!
\q1 \v 6 Then I would not have shame
\q1 when I look to all of your commandments.
\q1 \v 7 I will thank you with uprightness of heart
\q1 when I learn the judgments of your righteousness.
\q1 \v 8 I will keep your statutes;
\q1 do not utterly leave me.
\qa BETH
\q1 \v 9 How can a young man keep his path pure?
\q1 By keeping according to your word.
\q1 \v 10 With all of my heart I seek you.
\q1 Do not let me stray from your commandments.
\q1 \v 11 I have hidden your word in my heart
\q1 so that I might not sin against you.
\q1 \v 12 Blessed {are} you, Yahweh;
\q1 teach me your statutes.
\q1 \v 13 With my lips I have recounted
\q1 all of the judgments of your mouth.
\q1 \v 14 I rejoice in the way of your testimonies
\q1 as upon all riches.
\q1 \v 15 I will meditate on your precepts
\q1 and I will study your paths.
\q1 \v 16 I delight in your statutes;
\q1 I will not forget your word.
\qa GIMEL
\q1 \v 17 Deal kindly with your servant
\q1 so that I may live and keep your word.
\q1 \v 18 Uncover my eyes so that I may gaze
\q1 on the marvelous things from your teaching.
\q1 \v 19 I am a sojourner in the land;
\q1 do not hide your commandments from me.
\q1 \v 20 My soul languishes with longing
\q1 for your judgments at all times.
\q1 \v 21 You rebuke the proud, the cursed,
\q1 those wandering from your commandments.
\q1 \v 22 Roll from upon me disgrace and humiliation,
\q1 for I have guarded your testimonies.
\q1 \v 23 Though rulers sit and discuss against me,
\q1 your servant meditates on your statutes.
\q1 \v 24 Indeed, your testimonies are my pleasure,
\q1 my men of counsel.
\qa DALETH
\q1 \v 25 My soul clings to the dust!
\q1 Revive me according to your word.
\q1 \v 26 I recounted my ways, and you answered me.
\q1 Teach me your statutes.
\q1 \v 27 Make me understand the way of your precepts,
\q1 so that I can meditate on your wonders.
\q1 \v 28 My soul melts from grief.
\q1 Lift me up by your word.
\q1 \v 29 Turn from me the path of deceit,
\q1 and favor me with your teaching.
\q1 \v 30 I have chosen the way of faithfulness;
\q1 I agree with your judgments.
\q1 \v 31 I cling to your testimonies;
\q1 Yahweh, do not let me be shamed.
\q1 \v 32 I run in the way of your commandments,
\q2 for you enlarge my heart.
\qa HE
\q1 \v 33 Teach me, Yahweh, the way of your statutes,
\q1 and I will keep it {to} the end.
\q1 \v 34 Give me understanding, and I will guard your teaching,
\q1 and I will keep it with a whole heart.
\q1 \v 35 Guide me in the path of your commandments,
\q1 for I delight in it.
\q1 \v 36 Incline my heart toward your testimonies
\q1 and not toward unrighteous gain.
\q1 \v 37 Turn away my eyes from looking at worthless things;
\q1 in your ways, revive me.
\q1 \v 38 Fulfill for your servant your word,
\q1 which {is} for the fear of you.
\q1 \v 39 Turn away my reproach, which I dread,
\q1 for your judgments are good.
\q1 \v 40 Behold, I long for your precepts!
\q1 In your righteousness, revive me!
\qa WAW
\q1 \v 41 And let your covenant faithfulness come to me, Yahweh;
\q1 your salvation, according to your word;
\q1 \v 42 then I will answer the one reproaching me {with} a word,
\q1 for I trust in your word.
\q1 \v 43 So do not utterly snatch the word of truth from my mouth,
\q1 for I wait for your judgments.
\q1 \v 44 Then I will observe your teaching continually,
\q1 forever and ever.
\q1 \v 45 And I will walk about in the broad,
\q1 for I seek your precepts.
\q1 \v 46 And I will speak of your testimonies before kings,
\q1 and I will not have shame.
\q1 \v 47 And I delight in your commandments,
\q1 which I love.
\q1 \v 48 And I will lift up my palms to your commandments, which I love,
\q1 and I will meditate on your statutes.
\qa ZAYIN
\q1 \v 49 Remember the word to your servant
\q1 by which you have given me hope.
\q1 \v 50 This {is} my comfort in my affliction
\q1 because your promise revives me.
\q1 \v 51 The proud utterly scoff at me;
\q1 from your teaching I do not turn aside.
\q1 \v 52 I remember your judgments from ancient times, Yahweh,
\q1 and I comfort myself.
\q1 \v 53 Rage has seized me
\q1 from the wicked rejecting your teaching.
\q1 \v 54 Your statutes are music to me
\q1 in the house of my sojourning.
\q1 \v 55 I remember your name during the night, Yahweh,
\q1 and I shall observe your teaching.
\q1 \v 56 This is for me,
\q1 that I keep your precepts.
\qa HETH
\q1 \v 57 Yahweh {is} my portion;
\q1 I promise to observe your words.
\q1 \v 58 I entreat your face with a whole heart;
\q1 be merciful to me according to your word.
\q1 \v 59 I examine my ways
\q1 and turn my feet to your testimonies.
\q1 \v 60 I hurry and do not delay
\q1 to observe your commandments.
\q1 \v 61 The cords of the wicked ensnare me;
\q1 I do not forget your teaching.
\q1 \v 62 In the middle of the night I rise to praise you
\q1 because of the judgments of your righteousness.
\q1 \v 63 I {am} a companion to all who fear you
\q1 and to observers of your precepts.
\q1 \v 64 Your covenant faithfulness fills the earth, Yahweh;
\q2 teach me your statutes.
\qa TETH
\q1 \v 65 You do good to your servant,
\q1 Yahweh, according to your word.
\q1 \v 66 Teach me good discernment and understanding,
\q1 for I trust in your commandments.
\q1 \v 67 Before I was afflicted, I was going astray,
\q1 but now I observe your word.
\q1 \v 68 You {are} good, and you do good.
\q1 Teach me your statutes.
\q1 \v 69 The arrogant smear lies on me;
\q1 I, with a whole heart, I keep your precepts.
\q1 \v 70 Their hearts {are} unfeeling like fat,
\q1 I, {in} your teaching, I delight.
\q1 \v 71 {It is} good for me that I have suffered
\q1 so that I would learn your statutes.
\q1 \v 72 The teaching of your mouth {is} good for me,
\q1 more than thousands of gold and silver.
\qa YODH
\q1 \v 73 Your hands have made me and established me;
\q1 give me understanding so that I may learn your commandments.
\q1 \v 74 May the fearful of you see me and rejoice
\q1 because I hope in your word.
\q1 \v 75 Yahweh, I know that your judgments {are} just,
\q1 and {in} faithfulness you humble me.
\q1 \v 76 Please may your covenant faithfulness be to comfort me,
\q1 according to your word to your servant.
\q1 \v 77 May your compassion come to me so that I may live,
\q1 for your teaching {is} my delight.
\q1 \v 78 Let the proud have shame,
\q1 for they have slandered me {with} a lie;
\q1 I, I will meditate on your precepts.
\q1 \v 79 May the fearful of you turn to me,
\q1 so that they may know your testimonies.
\q1 \v 80 May my heart be blameless in your statutes,
\q2 so that I may not have shame.
\qa KAPH
\q1 \v 81 My soul faints for your salvation!
\q1 I wait for your word.
\q1 \v 82 My eyes faint for your promise;
\q1 saying, “When will you comfort me?”
\q1 \v 83 For I have become like a wineskin in the smoke;
\q1 I do not forget your statutes.
\q1 \v 84 How many {are} the days of your servant?
\q1 When will you act in pursuing justice for me?
\q1 \v 85 The proud have dug pits for me,
\q1 which is not according to your teaching.
\q1 \v 86 All of your commandments are truth.
\q1 They pursue me {in} deceit; help me!
\q1 \v 87 As a little they have made an end of me in the land,
\q1 but I, I have not rejected your precepts.
\q1 \v 88 According to your covenant faithfulness, keep me alive,
\q1 so that I may observe the testimony of your mouth.
\qa LAMEDH
\q1 \v 89 Forever, Yahweh,
\q1 your word is established in the heavens.
\q1 \v 90 Your faithfulness {is} to generation and generation;
\q1 you have established the earth, and it stands.
\q1 \v 91 By your judgments, they stand today,
\q1 for all things are your servants.
\q1 \v 92 If your teaching {had} not {been} my delight,
\q1 then I would have perished in my affliction.
\q1 \v 93 I will not forget your precepts forever,
\q1 for through them you have preserved me alive.
\q1 \v 94 I am yours; save me,
\q1 for I seek your precepts.
\q1 \v 95 The wicked wait for me to destroy me;
\q1 I pay attention to your testimonies.
\q1 \v 96 I have seen an end for all perfection;
\q1 your commandment is very broad.
\qa MEM
\q1 \v 97 How I love your teaching!
\q1 It is my meditation all the day.
\q1 \v 98 Your commandment makes me wiser than my enemies,
\q1 for it is with me forever.
\q1 \v 99 I have more insight than all my teachers,
\q1 for your testimonies are a meditation to me.
\q1 \v 100 I understand more than the elders,
\q2 for I have kept your precepts.
\q1 \v 101 I have restrained my feet from every evil path,
\q2 so that I might keep your word.
\q1 \v 102 I have not turned aside from your judgments,
\q2 for you, you have taught me.
\q1 \v 103 How your word is sweet to my palate,
\q2 more than honey to my mouth!
\q1 \v 104 From your precepts I gain understanding;
\q2 therefore, I hate every path of falsehood.
\qa NUN
\q1 \v 105 Your word {is} a lamp to my foot
\q2 and a light to my path.
\q1 \v 106 I have sworn and I will confirm {it},
\q2 to keep the judgments of your righteousness.
\q1 \v 107 I have been afflicted exceedingly;
\q2 Yahweh, revive me according to your word.
\q1 \v 108 Please accept the freewill offerings of my mouth, Yahweh,
\q2 and teach me your judgments.
\q1 \v 109 My soul {is} in my palm continually,
\q2 but I do not forget your teaching.
\q1 \v 110 The wicked have set a snare for me,
\q2 but I have not wandered from your precepts.
\q1 \v 111 I have inherited your testimonies forever,
\q2 for they {are} the joy of my heart.
\q1 \v 112 I have inclined my heart to do your statutes
\q2 to forever, the end.
\qa SAMEKH
\q1 \v 113 The double-minded I have hated,
\q2 but your teaching I have loved.
\q1 \v 114 My hiding place and my shield {are} you;
\q2 for your word I wait.
\q1 \v 115 Turn aside from me, doers of evil,
\q2 and let me keep the commandments of my God.
\q1 \v 116 Sustain me according to your word so that I may live,
\q2 and do not make me ashamed of my hope.
\q1 \v 117 Support me so that I will be saved,
\q2 and so I may gaze on your statutes continually.
\q1 \v 118 You reject all those straying from your statutes,
\q2 for their deceit {is} falsehood.
\q1 \v 119 You cause to cease {as} dross all the wicked of the earth;
\q2 therefore, I love your testimonies.
\q1 \v 120 My flesh shudders from dread of you,
\q2 and I fear your judgments.
\qa AYIN
\q1 \v 121 I have done justice and righteousness;
\q2 do not leave me to those oppressing me.
\q1 \v 122 Be surety for your servant for good;
\q2 do not let the arrogant oppress me.
\q1 \v 123 My eyes have failed for your salvation
\q2 and for the word of your righteousness.
\q1 \v 124 Deal with your servant according to your covenant faithfulness,
\q2 and teach me your statutes.
\q1 \v 125 I {am} your servant; give me understanding,
\q2 so that I can know your testimonies.
\q1 \v 126 {It is} time for Yahweh to act;
\q2 they have broken your law.
\q1 \v 127 Therefore, I love your commandments
\q2 more than gold and more than fine gold.
\q1 \v 128 Therefore, all the precepts of everything I carefully observe;
\q2 every path of falsehood I hate.
\qa PE
\q1 \v 129 Your testimonies {are} wonderful;
\q2 therefore, my soul has kept them.
\q1 \v 130 The doorway of your words gives light,
\q2 giving understanding to the simple.
\q1 \v 131 I open wide my mouth and I pant,
\q2 for I long for your commandments.
\q1 \v 132 Turn to me and be gracious to me,
\q2 according to the judgment for the ones loving your name.
\q1 \v 133 Establish my steps in your word,
\q2 and do not let any iniquity rule over me.
\q1 \v 134 Redeem me from the oppression of man,
\q2 that I may keep your precepts.
\q1 \v 135 Make your face shine on your servant,
\q2 and teach me your statutes.
\q1 \v 136 Streams of water go down {from} my eyes,
\q2 because they do not keep your law.
\qa TSADE
\q1 \v 137 Righteous {are} you, Yahweh,
\q2 and upright {are} your judgments.
\q1 \v 138 You have commanded your testimonies {in} righteousness
\q2 and faithfulness exceedingly.
\q1 \v 139 My zeal consumes me,
\q2 for my adversaries have forgotten your words.
\q1 \v 140 Your word {is} refined exceedingly,
\q2 and your servant loves it.
\q1 \v 141 Small {am} I and despised;
\q2 your precepts I have not forgotten.
\q1 \v 142 Your righteousness {is} righteousness forever,
\q2 and your law {is} truth.
\q1 \v 143 Narrow and distress have found me;
\q2 your commandments {are} my delight.
\q1 \v 144 The righteousness of your testimonies {is} forever;
\q2 give me understanding, so that I may live.
\qa QOPH
\q1 \v 145 I call out with a whole heart; answer me, Yahweh!
\q2 I shall keep your statutes.
\q1 \v 146 I call out to you; save me,
\q2 so that I may keep your testimonies.
\q1 \v 147 I preempt the dawn and cry for help;
\q2 for your words I wait.
\q1 \v 148 My eyes preempt the night watches,
\q2 to meditate on your word.
\q1 \v 149 Hear my voice according to your covenant faithfulness;
\q2 Yahweh, according to your judgment, revive me.
\q1 \v 150 The pursuers of evil purpose have drawn near;
\q2 from your law they are far away.
\q1 \v 151 Near {are} you, Yahweh,
\q2 and all your commandments {are} truth.
\q1 \v 152 Long ago, I knew from your testimonies
\q2 that you have founded them forever.
\qa RESH
\q1 \v 153 See my affliction and rescue me,
\q2 for I have not forgotten your law.
\q1 \v 154 Plead my plea and redeem me;
\q2 for your word, revive me.
\q1 \v 155 Salvation {is} far from the wicked,
\q2 for they have not sought your statutes.
\q1 \v 156 Your compassions {are} many, Yahweh;
\q2 according to your judgments, revive me.
\q1 \v 157 Many {are} my pursuers and my adversaries;
\q2 from your testimonies I do not turn aside.
\q1 \v 158 I have seen the treacherous, and I was disgusted,
\q2 because they have not kept your word.
\q1 \v 159 See that I have loved your precepts;
\q2 Yahweh, according to your covenant faithfulness, revive me.
\q1 \v 160 The head of your word {is} truth,
\q2 and every judgment of your righteousness {is} forever.
\qa SHIN
\q1 \v 161 Princes pursue me without cause,
\q2 and my heart trembles from your words.
\q1 \v 162 I am rejoicing over your word,
\q2 like one finding great plunder.
\q1 \v 163 Falsehood I hate and I abhor;
\q2 your law I love.
\q1 \v 164 Seven times in the day I praise you,
\q2 because of the judgments of your righteousness.
\q1 \v 165 Great peace {is} to the ones loving your law,
\q2 and there is no stumbling block for them.
\q1 \v 166 I hope for your salvation, Yahweh,
\q2 and I do your commandments.
\q1 \v 167 My soul keeps your testimonies,
\q2 and I love them exceedingly.
\q1 \v 168 I keep your precepts and your testimonies,
\q2 for all my ways {are} before you.
\qa TAV
\q1 \v 169 May my cry come near to your face, Yahweh;
\q2 according to your word, give me understanding.
\q1 \v 170 May my plea come to your face;
\q2 according to your word, deliver me.
\q1 \v 171 May my lips gush out praise,
\q2 for you teach me your statutes.
\q1 \v 172 May my tongue sing of your word,
\q2 for all your commandments {are} righteousness.
\q1 \v 173 May your hand be to help me,
\q2 for I have chosen your precepts.
\q1 \v 174 I long for your salvation, Yahweh,
\q2 and your law {is} my delight.
\q1 \v 175 May my soul live, and may it praise you,
\q2 and may your judgments help me.
\q1 \v 176 I have strayed like a perishing sheep;
\q2 seek your servant, for I have not forgotten your commandments.
\c 120
\d
\q1 \v 1 \d A song of ascents.
\q1 To Yahweh, in the distress to me,
\q2 I called, and he answered me.
\q1 \v 2 Yahweh, deliver my soul
\q2 from a lip of falsehood,
\q2 from a tongue of deceit.
\q1 \v 3 What will he give to you, and what will he add to you,
\q2 O tongue of deceit?
\q1 \v 4 Arrows of a warrior, sharpened,
\q2 with coals of broom trees.
\q1 \v 5 Woe to me, for I am sojourning {in} Meshech;
\q2 I am dwelling with the tents of Kedar.
\q1 \v 6 My soul has dwelt much to itself
\q2 with a hater of peace.
\q1 \v 7 I {am} peace, but when I speak,
\q2 they {are} for war.
\c 121
\d
\q1 \v 1 \d A song of ascents.
\q1 I lift up my eyes to the mountains.
\q2 From where does my help come?
\q1 \v 2 My help {is} from with Yahweh,
\q2 maker of heaven and earth.
\q1 \v 3 May he not give your foot to the slipping;
\q2 may your keeper not slumber.
\q1 \v 4 Behold, he will not slumber,
\q2 and he will not sleep,
\q2 the keeper of Israel.
\q1 \v 5 Yahweh {is} your keeper;
\q2 Yahweh {is} your shade upon your right hand.
\q1 \v 6 By day the sun will not strike you,
\q2 and the moon by night.
\q1 \v 7 Yahweh will keep you from all evil;
\q2 he will keep your soul.
\q1 \v 8 Yahweh will keep your going out and your coming in,
\q2 from now and to forever.
\c 122
\q1 \v 1 \d A song of ascents; of David.
\q1 I rejoiced in the ones saying to me, “Let us go {to} the house of Yahweh.”
\q1 \v 2 Our feet are standing
\q2 in your gates, Jerusalem.
\q1 \v 3 Jerusalem, the one built
\q2 like a city that is joined to itself together.
\q1 \v 4 Where the tribes go up,
\q2 the tribes of Yah,
\q2 a testimony to Israel,
\q2 to give thanks to the name of Yahweh.
\q1 \v 5 For there sit thrones for judgment,
\q2 thrones for the house of David.
\q1 \v 6 Ask {for} the peace of Jerusalem;
\q2 may the ones loving you prosper.
\q1 \v 7 Let there be peace within your rampart,
\q2 prosperity in your citadels.
\q1 \v 8 For the sake of my brothers and my companions,
\q2 let me speak, please, peace in you.
\q1 \v 9 For the sake of the house of Yahweh our God,
\q2 let me seek good for you.
\c 123
\q1 \v 1 \d A song of ascents.
\q1 To you I lift up my eyes,
\q2 the one dwelling in the heavens.
\q1 \v 2 Behold, as the eyes of servants {are} to the hand of their masters,
\q2 as the eyes of a maidservant {are} to the hand of her mistress,
\q2 thus our eyes {are} to Yahweh our God,
\q2 until he is gracious to us.
\q1 \v 3 Be gracious to us, Yahweh, be gracious to us,
\q2 for we are greatly satiated with contempt.
\q1 \v 4 Greatly our soul is
\q2 satiated with it, the scorn of the arrogant,
\q2 the contempt of the proud.
\c 124
\q1 \v 1 \d A song of ascents; of David.
\q1 If not Yahweh who was for us—
\q2 let Israel indeed say—
\q1 \v 2 if not Yahweh who was for us
\q2 when man rose up against us,
\q1 \v 3 then they would have swallowed us alive
\q2 when their nose burned against us.
\q1 \v 4 Then the waters would have overflowed us;
\q2 the torrent would have passed over our soul.
\q1 \v 5 Then the raging waters would have passed over our soul.
\q1 \v 6 Blessed {be} Yahweh,
\q2 who did not make us prey for their teeth.
\q1 \v 7 Our soul {is} like a bird {that} escaped from the snare of the trappers;
\q2 the snare was broken, and we, we escaped.
\q1 \v 8 Our help {is} in the name of Yahweh,
\q2 the maker of heaven and earth.
\c 125
\q1 \v 1 \d A song of ascents.
\q1 Those trusting in Yahweh {are} like Mount Zion;
\q2 it will not be shaken; forever it abides.
\q1 \v 2 Jerusalem—mountains {are} around her,
\q2 and Yahweh {is} around his people,
\q2 from now and to forever.
\q1 \v 3 For the rod of wickedness will not rest on the lot of the righteous,
\q2 so that the righteous will not stretch out their hands in unrighteousness.
\q1 \v 4 Do good, Yahweh, to the good,
\q2 and to the upright in their hearts.
\q1 \v 5 And those twisting their crooked {ways},
\q2 Yahweh will make them go with the workers of iniquity.
\q1 Peace {be} upon Israel.
\c 126
\q1 \v 1 \d A song of ascents.
\q1 When Yahweh returned the captivity of Zion,
\q2 we were like ones dreaming.
\q1 \v 2 Then our mouth was filled {with} laughter,
\q2 and our tongue {with} a shout of joy.
\q1 Then they said among the nations,
\q2 “Yahweh has made great to do with these.”
\q1 \v 3 Yahweh has made great to do with us;
\q2 we are joyful.
\q1 \v 4 Return, Yahweh, our captivity,
\q2 like the streams in the Negev.
\q1 \v 5 The ones sowing in tears
\q2 will reap in a shout of joy.
\q1 \v 6 Going, he may go and weeping,
\q2 carrying the bag of seed.
\q1 Coming, he will come in a shout of joy,
\q2 carrying his sheaves.
\c 127
\q1 \v 1 \d A song of ascents; of Solomon.
\q1 If Yahweh does not build a house,
\q2 {in} vain its builders have labored on it.
\q1 If Yahweh does not watch a city,
\q2 {in} vain the watchman has stayed awake.
\q1 \v 2 {It is} vain for you, the ones rising early to get up,
\q2 the ones being late to sit down,
\q2 the ones eating the bread of toils;
\q1 certainly he gives to his beloved one sleep.
\q1 \v 3 Behold, the inheritance of Yahweh {is} sons;
\q2 a reward {is} the fruit of the womb.
\q1 \v 4 Like arrows in the hand of a warrior,
\q2 thus {are} the sons of the youth.
\q1 \v 5 The happinesses of the man who has filled his quiver of them!
\q2 They will not have shame
\q2 when they speak with adversaries in the gate.
\c 128
\q1 \v 1 \d A song of ascents.
\q1 The happinesses of everyone fearing Yahweh,
\q2 the one walking in his ways.
\q1 \v 2 The labor of your palms, when you eat {it},
\q2 {is} your happiness, and good for you.
\q1 \v 3 Your wife {is} like a fruitful vine
\q2 in the recesses of your house.
\q1 Your sons {are} like shoots of olive trees,
\q2 all around your table.
\q1 \v 4 Behold, for thus the man fearing Yahweh will be blessed.
\q1 \v 5 May Yahweh bless you from Zion,
\q2 that you may look on the good of Jerusalem
\q2 all of the days of your life,
\q1 \v 6 and that you may see sons to your sons.
\q2 Peace {be} upon Israel!
\c 129
\q1 \v 1 \d A song of ascents.
\q1 Abundantly they have afflicted me from my youth.
\q2 Let Israel indeed say:
\q1 \v 2 Abundantly they have afflicted me from my youth;
\q2 however, they did not prevail against me.
\q1 \v 3 Upon my back the plowers plowed;
\q2 they made long their furrows.
\q1 \v 4 Yahweh {is} righteous;
\q2 he has cut the cords of the wicked.
\q1 \v 5 Let them have shame and withdraw backward,
\q2 all the haters of Zion.
\q1 \v 6 Let them be like grass of the rooftops,
\q2 that before one pulls {it} out, it dries up,
\q1 \v 7 that the reaper does not fill his palm {with},
\q2 and the one binding sheaves, {does} not fill his bosom,
\q1 \v 8 and those passing by do not say, “The blessing of Yahweh {be} upon you;
\q2 we bless you in the name of Yahweh.”
\c 130
\q1 \v 1 \d A song of ascents.
\q1 Out of the depths I cry to you, Yahweh.
\q1 \v 2 Lord, hear my voice;
\q1 let your ears be attentive
\q1 to the voice of my supplications.
\q1 \v 3 If you, Yah, would mark sins,
\q1 Lord, who could stand?
\q1 \v 4 However, {there is} forgiveness with you,
\q1 so that you may be feared.
\q1 \v 5 I wait for Yahweh; my soul waits,
\q1 and in his word I hope;
\q1 \v 6 my soul for the Lord,
\q1 more than watchmen for the morning,
\q2 watchmen for the morning.
\q1 \v 7 Israel, hope in Yahweh,
\q1 for with Yahweh {is} covenant faithfulness,
\q1 and with him {is} abundant redemption.
\q1 \v 8 And he, he will redeem Israel
\q1 from all his sins.
\c 131
\q1 \v 1 \d A song of ascents; of David.
\q1 Yahweh, my heart is not high and my eyes are not raised up,
\q2 and I do not walk in great and marvelous {things} beyond me.
\q1 \v 2 Rather, I have stilled and quieted my soul
\q1 like a weaned child upon his mother;
\q1 like a weaned child upon me {is} my soul.
\q1 \v 3 Israel, hope in Yahweh
\q1 from now and until forever!
\c 132
\q1 \v 1 \d A song of ascents.
\q1 Remember, Yahweh, for David,
\q2 all of his afflictions,
\q1 \v 2 who swore to
\q2 Yahweh; vowed to the Mighty One of Jacob,
\q1 \v 3 “If I go into the tent of my house,
\q2 if I go up on the bed of my couch,
\q1 \v 4 if I give sleep to my eyes,
\q2 slumber to my eyelids,
\q1 \v 5 until I find a place for Yahweh,
\q2 dwellings for the Mighty One of Jacob.”
\q1 \v 6 Behold, we heard of it in Ephrathah;
\q2 we found it in the fields of Jaar.
\q1 \v 7 “Let us go to his dwellings;
\q2 let us bow down at the footstool of his feet.”
\q1 \v 8 Arise, Yahweh, to your resting place,
\q2 you and the box of your strength.
\q1 \v 9 Let your priests wear righteousness,
\q2 and let your faithful shout for joy.
\q1 \v 10 For the sake of David your servant,
\q2 do not turn back the face of your anointed.
\q1 \v 11 Yahweh swore to David,
\q2 {in} truth, he will not turn back from it:
\q1 “From the fruit of your body
\q2 I will set {one} on the throne for you.
\q1 \v 12 If your sons keep my covenant
\q2 and my testimonies that I will teach them,
\q2 then also their sons, unto perpetuity,
\q2 will sit on the throne for you.”
\q1 \v 13 For Yahweh has chosen Zion;
\q2 he desired {it} for a dwelling for himself.
\q1 \v 14 “This {is} my resting place unto perpetuity;
\q2 here I will dwell, for I have desired it.
\q1 \v 15 Blessing I will bless her provisions;
\q2 her needy I will satisfy {with} bread.
\q1 \v 16 And her priests I will clothe {with} salvation,
\q2 and her faithful, shouting they will shout for joy.
\q1 \v 17 There I will make a horn sprout for David;
\q2 I have arranged a lamp for my anointed one.
\q1 \v 18 His enemies I will clothe {with} shame,
\q2 but upon him his crown will flourish.”
\c 133
\d
\v 1 A song of ascents; of David
\q1 Behold, how good and how pleasant
\q2 {is} the dwelling of brothers, yes, together!
\q1 \v 2 Like the good oil on the head,
\q2 coming down on the beard, the beard of Aaron,
\q2 that is coming down on the mouth of his garments,
\q1 \v 3 like the dew of Hermon
\q2 that is coming down on the mountains of Zion,
\q2 for there Yahweh commanded the blessing,
\q2 life to forever.
\c 134
\d
\v 1 A song of the ascents.
\q1 Behold, bless Yahweh,
\q2 all servants of Yahweh,
\q2 the ones standing in the house of Yahweh in the nights.
\q1 \v 2 Lift up your hands {to the} holiness,
\q2 and bless Yahweh.
\q1 \v 3 May Yahweh bless you from Zion,
\q2 the maker of heaven and earth.
\c 135
\q1 \v 1 Hallelu Yah!
\q1 Praise the name of Yahweh;
\q2 praise {him}, servants of Yahweh,
\q1 \v 2 who are standing in the house of Yahweh,
\q2 in the courts of the house of our God.
\q1 \v 3 Hallelu Yah, for Yahweh {is} good;
\q2 make music to his name, for {it is} pleasant.
\q1 \v 4 For Yah chose Jacob for himself;
\q2 Israel for his special possession.
\q1 \v 5 For I, I know that Yahweh {is} great,
\q2 and our Lord than all gods.
\q1 \v 6 Everything that Yahweh desires, he does,
\q2 in the heavens and on the earth,
\q2 in the seas and all deeps—
\q1 \v 7 bringing up clouds from the end of the earth,
\q2 he makes lightning bolts for the rain—
\q2 bringing out wind from his storehouses,
\q1 \v 8 who struck the firstborn of Egypt,
\q2 from man to beast.
\q1 \v 9 He sent signs and wonders
\q2 into your midst, Egypt,
\q2 against Pharaoh and against all of his servants,
\q1 \v 10 who struck many nations
\q2 and slew mighty kings:
\q1 \v 11 Sihon, king of the Amorite,
\q2 and Og, king of the Bashan,
\q2 and all the kingdoms of Canaan.
\q1 \v 12 And he gave their land {as} an inheritance,
\q2 an inheritance for Israel, his people.
\q1 \v 13 Yahweh, your name {is} to forever;
\q2 Yahweh, your remembrance {is} to generation and generation.
\q1 \v 14 For Yahweh vindicates his people,
\q2 and he has compassion on his servants.
\q1 \v 15 The idols of the nations {are} silver and gold,
\q2 the work of the hands of man.
\q1 \v 16 A mouth {is} to them, but they do not speak;
\q2 eyes {are} to them, but they do not see.
\q1 \v 17 Ears {are} to them, but they do not listen;
\q2 indeed there is no breath in their mouths.
\q1 \v 18 Their makers are like them—
\q2 everyone who is trusting in them.
\q1 \v 19 House of Israel, bless Yahweh;
\q2 house of Aaron, bless Yahweh.
\q1 \v 20 House of the Levite, bless Yahweh;
\q2 fearers of Yahweh, bless Yahweh!
\q1 \v 21 Blessed {be} Yahweh from Zion,
\q2 the one dwelling {in} Jerusalem.
\q1 Hallelu Yah!
\c 136
\q1 \v 1 Give thanks to Yahweh, for {he} is good,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 2 Give thanks to the God of the gods,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 3 Give thanks to the Lord of the lords,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 4 To the doer of great wonders, him alone,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 5 To the maker of the heavens by understanding,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 6 To the one spreading out the earth over the waters,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 7 To the maker of great lights,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever,
\q1 \v 8 the sun for dominion in the day,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever,
\q1 \v 9 the moon and stars for dominion in the night,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 10 To the striker of Egypt in their firstborn,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 11 And he brought out Israel from their midst,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 12 By a strong hand and by an outstretched arm,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 13 To the parter of the Sea of Reeds into parts,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 14 And he made Israel pass through the midst of it,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 15 And he tossed Pharaoh and his army into the Sea of Reeds,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 16 To the one leading his people in the wilderness,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 17 To the one striking great kings,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 18 And he killed mighty kings,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever,
\q1 \v 19 Sihon, king of the Amorite,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever,
\q1 \v 20 and Og, king of the Bashan,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 21 And he gave their land as an inheritance,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever,
\q1 \v 22 an inheritance to Israel his servant,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever,
\q1 \v 23 who, in our humiliation, remembered us,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 24 And he tore us away from our adversaries,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever,
\q1 \v 25 giving bread to all of flesh,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever.
\q1 \v 26 Give thanks to the God of the heavens,
\q2 for his covenant faithfulness {is} to forever!
\c 137
\q1 \v 1 By the rivers of Babylon,
\q2 there we sat down, also we wept,
\q2 when we remembered Zion.
\q1 \v 2 On the willows in her midst
\q2 we hung our harps.
\q1 \v 3 For there our captors requested of us
\q2 words of a song,
\q1 and our tormentors, joy: “Sing for us from a song of Zion.”
\q1 \v 4 How shall we sing the song of Yahweh
\q2 on the land of foreignness?
\q1 \v 5 If I forget you, Jerusalem,
\q2 let my right hand forget.
\q1 \v 6 Let my tongue cling to my palate
\q2 if I do not remember you, if I do not cause Jerusalem to go up
\q2 above the head of my joy.
\q1 \v 7 Remember, Yahweh, for the sons of Edom,
\q2 the day of Jerusalem,
\q1 the ones saying, “Lay bare, lay bare,
\q2 to the foundation in her!”
\q1 \v 8 Daughter Babylon, the devastated one,
\q2 the happinesses of the one who makes complete to you
\q2 your repayment that you paid to us!
\q1 \v 9 The happinesses of the one who seizes
\q2 and dashes your infants
\q2 against the rock!
\c 138
\q1 \v 1 \d Of David
\q1 I will thank you with my whole heart;
\q2 before the gods I will make music to you.
\q1 \v 2 I will bow down toward the temple of your holiness,
\q1 and I will praise your name for your covenant faithfulness and for your trustworthiness,
\q1 for you have exalted above all of your name your word.
\q1 \v 3 On the day that I called and you answered me,
\q1 you emboldened my soul {with} power.
\q1 \v 4 May all the kings of the earth thank you, Yahweh,
\q1 because they heard the words from your mouth.
\q1 \v 5 May they sing of the ways of Yahweh,
\q1 for great is the glory of Yahweh.
\q1 \v 6 Though Yahweh is high, yet he sees the lowly,
\q1 and the proud he knows from far off.
\q1 \v 7 Though I walk in the middle of trouble, you will keep me alive;
\q1 you will stretch out your hand against the nose of my enemies,
\q1 and your right hand will save me.
\q1 \v 8 Yahweh will accomplish for my benefit;
\q1 your covenant faithfulness, Yahweh, {is} forever.
\q1 Do not forsake the works of your hands.
\c 139
\p
\v 1 \d For the chief musician; of David; a psalm.
\q1 Yahweh, you have searched me
\q2 and you know {me}.
\q1 \v 2 You, you know my sitting down and my rising up;
\q2 you understand my thought from far away.
\q1 \v 3 My path and my lying down you have winnowed,
\q2 and you are familiar with all of my ways.
\q1 \v 4 For there is not a word on my tongue;
\q2 behold, Yahweh, you know all of it.
\q1 \v 5 Behind and before you have enclosed me,
\q2 and you have set your palm upon me.
\q1 \v 6 {Such} knowledge {is} too wonderful for me;
\q2 it is high; I am not capable of it.
\q1 \v 7 Where shall I go from your spirit?
\q2 And where shall I flee from your face?
\q1 \v 8 If I ascend {to} the heavens, you {are} there,
\q2 and I spread out {in} Sheol, behold, you!
\q1 \v 9 {If} I lift up the wings of the dawn,
\q2 dwell in the farthest part of the sea,
\q1 \v 10 even there your hand will lead me,
\q2 and your right hand will hold me.
\q1 \v 11 And I said, “Surely darkness will crush me,
\q2 and night, the light around me.”
\q1 \v 12 Even darkness does not make it dark to you,
\q2 and the night shines like the day;
\q2 like darkness, like light.
\q1 \v 13 For you, you created my kidneys;
\q2 you knit me together in the womb of my mother.
\q1 \v 14 I will thank you because fearsomely,
\q2 I am wonderfully made.
\q1 Wonderful {are} your works,
\q2 and my soul knows {it} very well.
\q1 \v 15 My frame was not hidden from you
\q2 when I was made in the secret place, {when} I was woven in the depths of the earth,
\q1 \v 16 your eyes saw my unformed substance.
\q2 And in your book all of them were written:
\q1 the days were formed,
\q2 and {yet} not one of them {was}.
\q1 \v 17 And to me, how precious are your thoughts, God!
\q2 How numerous are their heads!
\q1 \v 18 {If} I should count them, they are more than the sand.
\q2 I awake, and I {am} still with you.
\q1 \v 19 If only you would kill the wicked, God!
\q2 And men of bloodshed, depart from me,
\q1 \v 20 who speak of you for an evil purpose;
\q2 they lift up {your name} to emptiness—your enemies.
\q1 \v 21 Do I not hate the ones hating you, Yahweh?
\q2 And do I not loathe the ones rising up against you?
\q1 \v 22 {With} a completeness of hatred I hate them;
\q2 they have become enemies to me.
\q1 \v 23 Search me, God, and know my heart;
\q2 examine me and know my cares.
\q1 \v 24 And see if a way of hurtfulness {is} in me,
\q2 and lead me in the way of eternity.
\c 140
\d For the chief musician; a psalm of David.
\q1 \v 1 Rescue me, Yahweh, from an evil man;
\q2 from a man of violence preserve me,
\q1 \v 2 who plot evil things in the heart;
\q2 all the day they travel around {to} battles.
\q1 \v 3 They have sharpened their tongue like a serpent;
\q2 venom of a viper {is} under their lips.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\b
\q1 \v 4 Guard me, Yahweh, from the hands of the wicked;
\q2 from the man of violence preserve me,
\q1 who have planned to push down my steps.
\q1 \v 5 The proud have hidden a snare for me, and cords;
\q2 they have spread out a net to the hand of the path;
\q2 traps they have set for me.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\b
\q1 \v 6 I have said to Yahweh, “You {are} my God.”
\q2 Give ear, Yahweh, to the voice of my supplications.
\q1 \v 7 Yahweh, Lord, the strength of my salvation,
\q2 you have covered my head in the day of weaponry.
\b
\q1 \v 8 Do not grant, Yahweh, the desires of the wicked;
\q2 do not bring forth his plot, {lest} they rise up.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\b
\q1 \v 9 The head of the ones surrounding me—
\q2 let the mischief of their lips cover them.
\q1 \v 10 Let burning coals fall on them;
\q2 let him cast them into the fire,
\q2 into pits, let them not rise up.
\b
\q1 \v 11 Let not a man of tongue be established in the land;
\q2 a man of violence—let evil hunt him with blows.
\b
\q1 \v 12 I know that Yahweh will do the cause of the poor,
\q2 the justice of the needy.
\q1 \v 13 Surely the righteous will praise your name;
\q2 the upright will dwell before your face.
\c 141
\q1 \v 1 \d A psalm of David
\q1 Yahweh, I cry out to you, “Hurry to me!
\q2 Give ear to my voice when I cry out to you.”
\q1 \v 2 May my prayer be established {like} incense to your face,
\q1 a raising of my palms {like} the evening sacrifice.
\q1 \v 3 Yahweh, place a guard over my mouth;
\q1 guard the door of my lips.
\q1 \v 4 Do not turn my heart toward an evil thing
\q1 to wantonly act in activities in wickedness
\q1 with men, doers of evil.
\q1 And may I not dine on their delicacies.
\q1 \v 5 Let the righteous hit me—covenant faithfulness, and he is correcting me!
\q1 Oil for the head may my head not refuse.
\q1 For my prayer {is} continually against their wickedness.
\q1 \v 6 Their judges are thrown down beside a cliff;
\q1 and they hear my words, that they are pleasant.
\q1 \v 7 “Just as splitting and breaking up in the ground,
\q1 our bones are scattered at the mouth of Sheol.”
\q1 \v 8 Yet my eyes are on you, Yahweh, Lord;
\q1 in you I take refuge; do not uncover my soul.
\q1 \v 9 Keep me from the hands of the snare they have laid for me,
\q1 and the traps of the workers of evil.
\q1 \v 10 Let the wicked fall into his nets together,
\q1 I, while I cross over.
\c 142
\d A maskil of David; when he was in the cave; a prayer.
\q1 \v 1 My voice to Yahweh—I cry out;
\q1 my voice to Yahweh—I plead for favor.
\q1 \v 2 I pour out my lament to his face;
\q1 my distress to his face I declare.
\q1 \v 3 When my spirit faints within me,
\q1 then you, you know my path.
\q1 Along this path I walk
\q1 they have hidden a trap for me.
\q1 \v 4 Look right and see
\q1 and there is no one who recognizes me.
\q1 A refuge has become lost from me;
\q1 there is no one caring for my soul.
\q1 \v 5 I cried out to you, Yahweh;
\q1 I said, “You {are} my shelter,
\q1 my portion in the land of the living.”
\q1 \v 6 Listen to my cry,
\q1 for I am very low;
\q1 rescue me from my pursuers,
\q1 for they are stronger than I.
\q1 \v 7 Bring out my soul from prison
\q1 to praise your name.
\q1 The righteous will gather around me
\q1 because you will fulfill for me.
\c 143
\q1 \v 1 \d A psalm of David
\q1 Hear my prayer, Yahweh; listen to my pleas!
\q2 On account of your faithfulness answer me in your righteousness!
\q1 \v 2 And do not enter into judgment with your servant,
\q1 for everyone living is not righteous to your face.
\q1 \v 3 For the enemy has pursued my soul;
\q1 he has crushed my life to the ground;
\q1 he has made me to live in dark places
\q1 like the dead of ages.
\q1 \v 4 So my spirit faints within me;
\q1 my heart despairs inside me.
\q1 \v 5 I remember days from before;
\q1 I meditate on all your works;
\q1 I reflect on the works of your hands.
\q1 \v 6 I spread out my hands to you;
\q1 my soul, as a thirsty land, to you.
\qs Selah
\qs*
\q1 \v 7 Hurry! Answer me, Yahweh; my spirit is expiring!
\q1 Do not hide your face from me,
\q1 or I will become equal with those going down to the pit.
\q1 \v 8 Let me hear your covenant faithfulness in the morning,
\q1 for I trust in you.
\q1 Make known to me this way I should walk,
\q1 for I lift up my soul to you.
\q1 \v 9 Rescue me from my enemies, Yahweh;
\q1 I hide in you.
\q1 \v 10 Teach me to do your will,
\q1 for you {are} my God.
\q1 May your good Spirit
\q1 lead me in a level land.
\q1 \v 11 Yahweh, for the sake of your name, may you preserve my life;
\q1 in your righteousness may you bring my soul out of distress.
\q1 \v 12 And in your covenant faithfulness may you destroy my enemies
\q1 and exterminate all the adversaries of my soul,
\q1 for I am your servant.
\c 144
\p
\v 1 \d Of David.
\q1 Blessed {be} Yahweh, my rock,
\q2 the one teaching my hands for war,
\q2 my fingers for battle,
\q1 \v 2 my covenant faithfulness and my fortress,
\q2 my stronghold and the one rescuing me,
\q1 my shield, and in whom I take refuge,
\q2 the one subduing my people under me.
\q1 \v 3 Yahweh, what {is} man, that you know him,
\q2 the son of man, that you consider him?
\q1 \v 4 Man compares to vapor;
\q2 his days {are} like a passing shadow.
\q1 \v 5 Yahweh, bow your heavens and come down;
\q2 touch the mountains, that they may smoke.
\q1 \v 6 Light lightning and scatter them;
\q2 send your arrows and rout them.
\q1 \v 7 Send your hands from above;
\q2 break me free and deliver me from many waters,
\q2 from the hand of sons of a foreigner,
\q1 \v 8 who, their mouth speaks worthlessness,
\q2 and their right hand {is} a right hand of falsehood.
\q1 \v 9 God, I will sing a new song to you;
\q2 with a lyre of ten {strings} I will make music to you,
\q1 \v 10 the one giving salvation to kings,
\q2 the one breaking free David his servant
\q2 from the evil sword.
\q1 \v 11 Break me free and deliver me
\q2 from the hand of the sons of a foreigner,
\q1 who, their mouth speaks worthlessness,
\q2 and their right hand {is} a right hand of falsehood,
\q1 \v 12 that our sons {may be} like plants
\q2 having been enlarged in their youth,
\q1 our daughters, like corner pillars
\q2 carved {in} the pattern of a palace.
\q1 \v 13 {May} our granaries {be} full,
\q2 furnishing from kind to kind;
\q1 may our flocks be thousanding,
\q2 may they be myriading in our fields.
\q1 \v 14 {May} our oxen {be} burdened;
\q2 no breach and no going out
\q2 and no cry in our squares.
\q1 \v 15 The happinesses of the people for whom {it is} thus to it!
\q2 The happinesses of the people for whom Yahweh {is} its God!
\c 145
\p
\v 1 \d A psalm of David.
\q1 I will exalt you, my God, the King,
\q2 and I will bless your name forever and ever.
\q1 \v 2 I will bless you every day,
\q2 and I will praise your name forever and ever.
\q1 \v 3 Yahweh {is} great and being much praised,
\q2 and there is no searching of his greatness.
\q1 \v 4 Generation to generation will proclaim your works,
\q2 and they will declare your mighty acts.
\q1 \v 5 {On} the splendor of the glory of your majesty
\q2 and {on} the deeds of your making wonderful, let me meditate.
\q1 \v 6 And they will tell the strength of your making fearful,
\q2 and let me recount it, your greatness.
\q1 \v 7 They will pour forth the remembrance of the abundance of your goodness,
\q2 and they will sing joyfully {about} your righteousness.
\q1 \v 8 Yahweh {is} gracious and compassionate,
\q2 long of nostrils and great of covenant faithfulness.
\q1 \v 9 Yahweh {is} good to all,
\q2 and his compassions {are} over all of his works.
\q1 \v 10 All your works will thank you, Yahweh,
\q2 and your faithful will bless you.
\q1 \v 11 They will tell the glory of your kingdom,
\q2 and they will speak {of} your power,
\q1 \v 12 to make known to the sons of man his mighty acts
\q2 and the glory of the splendor of his kingdom.
\q1 \v 13 Your kingdom {is} a kingdom of all of eternities,
\q2 and your dominion {is} in every generation and generation.
\q1 \v 14 Yahweh is supporting all of the ones falling
\q2 and raising up all of the ones being bowed down.
\q1 \v 15 The eyes of all wait for you,
\q2 and you, you are giving their food to them in its time,
\q1 \v 16 opening your hand
\q2 and satisfying every living {thing} {with respect to} desire.
\q1 \v 17 Yahweh {is} righteous in all of his ways
\q2 and faithful in all of his works.
\q1 \v 18 Yahweh {is} near to all of the ones calling on him,
\q2 to all who call on him in truth.
\q1 \v 19 He does the desire of the ones fearing him,
\q2 and he hears their cry, and he saves them.
\q1 \v 20 Yahweh is keeping all of the ones loving him,
\q2 but he destroys all of the wicked.
\q1 \v 21 My mouth will speak the praise of Yahweh,
\q2 and all flesh will bless the name of his holiness forever and ever.
\c 146
\q1 \v 1 Hallelu Yah!
\q2 Praise Yahweh, my soul!
\q1 \v 2 Let me praise Yahweh in my life;
\q2 let me make music to my God while I yet {am}.
\q1 \v 3 Do not trust in nobles,
\q2 in the son of man, in whom there is no salvation.
\q1 \v 4 His breath goes out, he returns to his ground;
\q2 on that day, his thoughts perish.
\q1 \v 5 The happinesses of {the one} who {has} the God of Jacob for his help;
\q2 his hope {is} in Yahweh his God,
\q1 \v 6 the one having made the heavens and the earth,
\q2 the sea and all that {is} in them,
\q2 the one keeping faithfulness forever,
\q1 \v 7 doing justice for the oppressed,
\q2 giving bread to the hungry.
\q2 Yahweh is releasing the bound ones.
\q1 \v 8 Yahweh is opening the blind;
\q2 Yahweh is raising up the one bowed down;
\q2 Yahweh is loving the righteous.
\q1 \v 9 Yahweh is guarding the sojourners;
\q2 he upholds the orphan and the widow,
\q2 but the way of the wicked, he overturns.
\q1 \v 10 Yahweh reigns forever;
\q2 your God, Zion, to generation and generation.
\q1 Hallelu Yah!
\c 147
\q1 \v 1 Hallelu Yah!
\q1 For {it is} good to make music {to} our God,
\q2 for praise {is} pleasant and suitable.
\q1 \v 2 Yahweh builds up Jerusalem;
\q2 he gathers the scattered of Israel,
\q1 \v 3 healing the broken of heart
\q2 and binding up their wounds;
\q1 \v 4 counting the number of the stars,
\q2 he calls names to all of them.
\q1 \v 5 Great is our Lord, and abundant of power,
\q2 his understanding {is} without number.
\q1 \v 6 Yahweh is lifting up the poor,
\q2 bringing down the wicked to the ground.
\q1 \v 7 Sing to Yahweh with thanksgiving;
\q2 make music to our God with the harp,
\q1 \v 8 the one covering the heavens with clouds;
\q2 the one preparing rain for the earth,
\q2 the one making the mountains sprout with grass.
\q1 \v 9 He gives its food to the beast,
\q2 to the sons of the raven when they call.
\q1 \v 10 He does not delight in the strength of a horse;
\q2 he does not take pleasure {in} the legs of a man.
\q1 \v 11 Yahweh takes pleasure {in} the ones fearing him,
\q2 the ones hoping for his covenant faithfulness.
\q1 \v 12 Extol Yahweh, Jerusalem;
\q2 praise your God, Zion.
\q1 \v 13 For he strengthens the bars of your gates;
\q2 he blesses your sons in your midst.
\q1 \v 14 The one putting peace {at} your borders,
\q2 he satisfies you {with} the fat of wheat.
\q1 \v 15 The one sending his command {to} the earth,
\q2 his word runs to swiftness.
\q1 \v 16 The one making snow like wool,
\q2 he scatters frost like ashes.
\q1 \v 17 The one sending his hail like crumbs,
\q2 who can stand to the face of his cold?
\q1 \v 18 He sends his word, and he makes them melt;
\q2 he makes his wind blow, and the waters flow.
\q1 \v 19 He declared his word to Jacob,
\q2 his statutes and his judgments to Israel.
\q1 \v 20 He has not done this for any {other} nation,
\q2 and his judgments, they do not know them.
\q1 Hallelu Yah!
\c 148
\q1 \v 1 Hallelu Yah!
\q1 Praise Yahweh from the heavens;
\q2 praise him in the heights.
\q1 \v 2 Praise him, all of his angels;
\q2 praise him, all of his armies.
\q1 \v 3 Praise him, sun and moon;
\q2 praise him, all of the stars of light.
\q1 \v 4 Praise him, heavens of the heavens,
\q2 and the waters that {are} above the heavens.
\q1 \v 5 Let them praise the name of Yahweh,
\q2 for he, he commanded, and they were created.
\q1 \v 6 And he established them forever and ever;
\q2 he gave a decree, and it will not pass away.
\q1 \v 7 Praise Yahweh from the earth,
\q2 sea creatures and all depths,
\q1 \v 8 fire and hail, snow and vapor,
\q2 wind of tempest, doing his word,
\q1 \v 9 mountains and all hills,
\q2 tree of fruit and all cedars,
\q1 \v 10 the living {creature} and every beast,
\q2 the creeper and the bird of wing,
\q1 \v 11 kings of the earth and all peoples,
\q2 princes and all judges of the earth,
\q1 \v 12 young men and also young women,
\q2 old men with youths.
\q1 \v 13 Let them praise the name of Yahweh,
\q2 for his name alone is exalted;
\q2 his splendor {is} over the earth and the heavens.
\q1 \v 14 And he has raised up a horn for his people,
\q2 praise for all of his faithful,
\q2 for the sons of Israel, a people near to him.
\q1 Hallelu Yah!
\c 149
\q1 \v 1 Hallelu Yah!
\q1 Sing to Yahweh a new song,
\q2 his praise in the assembly of the faithful.
\q1 \v 2 Let Israel rejoice in his Maker;
\q2 let the sons of Zion be glad in their king.
\q1 \v 3 Let them praise his name in the dance;
\q2 let them make music to him with the tambourine and the harp.
\q1 \v 4 For Yahweh is taking pleasure in his people;
\q2 he beautifies the humble with salvation.
\q1 \v 5 Let the faithful exult in glory;
\q2 let them sing joyfully on their beds.
\q1 \v 6 {Let} the exaltations of God {be} in their throat,
\q2 and a sword of mouths in their hand,
\q1 \v 7 to execute vengeance on the nations,
\q2 punishments on the peoples,
\q1 \v 8 to bind their kings with chains
\q2 and their nobles with shackles of iron,
\q1 \v 9 to execute on them the judgment written.
\q2 It {is} honor to all of his faithful.
\q1 Hallelu Yah!
\c 150
\q1 \v 1 Hallelu Yah!
\q1 Praise God in his sanctuary;
\q2 praise him in the expanse of his strength.
\q1 \v 2 Praise him for his mighty deeds;
\q2 praise him according to the abundance of his greatness.
\q1 \v 3 Praise him with the blast of a shofar;
\q2 praise him with the lyre and the harp.
\q1 \v 4 Praise him with the tambourine and the dance;
\q2 praise him with stringed instruments and the flute.
\q1 \v 5 Praise him with cymbals of hearing;
\q2 praise him with cymbals of a shout.
\q1 \v 6 Let all of the breath praise Yah!
\q1 Hallelu Yah! 